\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Russian c.banker sees rouble free float in 2 years\b0\par\par\uc2 719 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juni 2009\par 12:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Russia \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  head sees rouble free float in 2 years\par \par \uc2 * Ignatyev expected to be re-appointed this week\par \par \uc2 * World Bank cuts Russian forecast for 2009\par \par \uc2 (Adds analyst quote, World Bank report, background)\par \par \uc2 By Dmitry Sergeyev and Gleb Bryanski\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, June 22 (Reuters) - Russia may float the rouble in two years but should continue \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  during the transition period, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  head said on Monday, outlining his policy vision for the next term.\par \par \uc2 Sergei Ignatyev, who steered the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  since 2002, overseeing accumulation of the world's third largest foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves and managing both appreciation and depreciation of the rouble, is expected to be re-appointed for a third term on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 A free float would enable the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to steer the economy through interest rates and may even make the rouble attractive as an international reserve \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  -- a cherished dream of the Russian leadership.\par \par \uc2 "Our main goal is a transition to an inflation targeting regime and (the rouble's) free float. I believe we can approach these decisions in the next two years," Ignatyev told parliament members during a committee hearing.\par \par \uc2 "I think we should not take any strict obligations in terms of stopping \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the next two years," Ignatyev said, adding that \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  was already half way towards a free float.\par \par \uc2 Analysts and policy makers have said the rouble decision will depend on Russia's current account balance and economic growth -- both heavily dependent on its oil and other commodity exports.\par \par \uc2 On Monday the World Bank cut its Russian forecast for this year to predict 7.5 percent contraction this year, down from an earlier forecast of 4.5 percent shrinkage. However, it revised up next year's forecast to 2.5 percent growth from stagnation.\par \par \uc2 POLITICAL SUPPORT\par \par \uc2 After devaluing the rouble by a third earlier this year, Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has set a wide trading band of between 26 and 41 roubles to a dollar/euro basket, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to iron out what it sees as excessive exchange rate volatility.\par \par \uc2 Ignatyev, a 61-year old technocrat and a former deputy to Finance Minister Alexei Kudrin, often faces criticism in parliament but with the firm backing of President Dmitry Medvedev his re-appointment is seen as a done deal.\par \par \uc2 Analysts see the re-appointment as a sign of gratitude from the country's leadership for the crisis management during the toughest weeks in September-October 2008 when the country's banking system was on the verge of collapse.\par \par \uc2 "The Chairman of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will work as long as he has support from the political leadership, it is not like in the Bank of England or the Fed," said Troika analyst Anton Tabakh. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is by law independent from the government.\par \par \uc2 A move to free float would be Russia's most significant economic decision since lifting capital movement restrictions in 2006, allowing the rouble to join the Brazilian real and South African rand among freely floating emerging \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 NO CONSENSUS\par \par \uc2 The move would require a legal change to formally charge the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  with controlling inflation as opposed to its current task of ensuring exchange rate stability.\par \par \uc2 There is no consensus between policy makers on the free float, with Ignatyev's own deputy Alexei Ulyukayev saying a free float is possible next year and Kremlin economic aide Arkady Dvorkovich saying a decision would be premature.\par \par \uc2 Russia's Prime Minister Vladimir Putin, seen as an ultimate decision-maker in Russia, has not yet spoken on the issue but has repeatedly said that the rouble should eventually become an international reserve \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The World Bank expects Russia's current account to remain in surplus equal to 3 percent of gross domestic product in 2010 after 2.4 percent in 2009, which should provide fundamental support for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 However, "possible oil price declines, the Russian banks' problems maturing into an acute form, or an emerging markets sell-off would be sufficient to weaken the rouble," said Alexander Morozov, \uc2 HSBC\uc2 's chief economist on Russia. (Writing by Gleb Bryanski, Editing by Ruth Pitchford)\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA-CBANK/IGNATYEV (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|C|D|E|M|O|U|MTL|GRO|SOF|OIL|ABX|BNX|FUN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090622e56m000pv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
