\par\par \b \uc2 Russian markets -- Factors to Watch on May 8\b0\par\par\uc2 749 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Mai 2009\par 08:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, May 8 (Reuters) - Here are events and news stories that could move Russian markets on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Russian markets will be closed on Monday, May 11 due to a public holiday.\par \par \uc2 You can reach us on: +7 495 775 1242\par \par \uc2 STOCKS CALL (Contributions to moscow.newsroom@reuters.com):\par \par \uc2 OTP -- There is a high probability of continued profit taking when the market is at a fairly elevated level. American bourses closed in the red.\par \par \uc2 Alor -- Today the main sell-off will be in the shares of recent rally leaders such as \uc2 Gazprom\uc2  , \uc2 Sberbank\uc2  and LUKOIL .\par \par \uc2 EVENTS [RU-DIA] (All times GMT):\par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON - U.S. President Barak Obama is expected to meet Russian Foreign Minister Sergei Lavrov\par \par \uc2 NEW YORK - Russian Foreign Minister Sergei Lavrov to participate in the meeting of UN Security Council on Middle East\par \par \uc2 SEOUL - A U.S. delegation led by special envoy to North Korea Stephen Bosworth visits South Korea to discuss ways to bring back Pyongyang to stalled six-party nuclear talks\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW - Moscow's envoy to NATO, Dmitry Rogozin, to participate in a video link between Moscow and Brussels (0730)\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW - Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to hold an auction for six-month collateral free loans for commercial banks, with 30 billion roubles on offer at a minimum bid rate of 14.75 percent\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW - Moscow Arbitration court to hear a motion filed by Norwegian telecoms group Telenor against enforcement of $1.7 billion case\par \par \uc2 IN THE PAPERS [PRESS/RU]:\par \par \uc2 Russian flag carrier Aeroflot will likely pay out no more than 500 million roubles in 2008 dividends -- less than the previously suggested 700 million roubles and equal to just a third of 2007's pay out, Vedomosti reports, citing a source on the company's board. The board recommended a dividend at a meeting this week but did not say how much. [ID:nL5718808]\par \par \uc2 Russian Railways saw freight volumes slump 22.7 percent last month, year-on-year, broadly at the same pace as in March, Kommersant writes. Passenger numbers fell 13.8 percent, it adds.\par \par \uc2 TOP STORIES IN RUSSIA AND THE CIS [RU-NEWS]: TOP NEWS: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Stocks, rouble rally to multi-month highs        [ID:nL7973599]\par  Clinton buries disputes for new Russia ties     [ID:nN07401576]\par  EU, church urge calm in Georgia after violence  [ID:nL71000458]\par  \par  COMPANIES/MARKETS:\par  VEB approves $578 mln subordinate loans to banks[ID:nL71027437]\par  CTC Q1 net dives 44 pct, shares rise             [ID:nL7997574]\par  Russia c.bank doubled dollar purchases in April   [ID:nL796004]\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sibirtelecom\f28 \uc2 \f2  proposes lower '08 dividend         [ID:nL7700794]\par  VEB to issue $10 bln foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bonds     [ID:nL71002835]\par  Banks must keep \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  debt under 20pct-cbanker      [ID:nL7938992]\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TNK-BP\f28 \uc2 \f2  employee convicted in \f28 \uc2 \f2 Gazprom\f28 \uc2 \f2  spying case [ID:nL7997403] ECONOMY/POLITICS: Few Russians believe Medvedev controls power-poll[ID:nL7935026] \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  EBRD sees 5.2 pct contraction for emrg Europe    [ID:nL7424503]\par  Russia to switch to cheaper steel coins         [ID:nL71009813]\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TABLE-Russian gold/\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 fx\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves rise to $385.9bln[ID:nMOS005432] ENERGY: RosGas buys Hungarian gas firm EMFESZ - spokesman[ID:nL7444981] \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Wary of Russia, EU wo