\par\par \b \uc2 Russian markets -- Factors to Watch on April 8\b0\par\par\uc2 789 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 April 2009\par 08:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, April 8 (Reuters) - Here are events and news stories that could move Russian markets on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 You can reach us on: +7 495 775 1242\par \par \uc2 STOCKS CALL (Contributions to moscow.newsroom@reuters.com):\par \par \uc2 Olma - Today at the start of trade, the RTS index is likely to correct deeper downwards, tracking oil prices and global stock markets...From the point of view of technical analysis, there are no signals for strong moves on the RTS for now.\par \par \uc2 VTB Capital - "Although this latest postponement of the long-awaited meeting with the government (from April 9 to an unspecified later date) is neutral for utilities stocks so far, any further delays and/or a lack of a decision over utilities' investment programmes and the long-term capacity market could start creating pressure on the stocks."\par \par \uc2 EVENTS [RU-DIA] (All times GMT): MOSCOW- First Deputy Prime Minister Igor Shuvalov to participate in a meeting of the government anti-crisis commission MOSCOW- Economic conference with Finance Minister Alexei Kudrin, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  First Deputy Chairman Alexei Ulyukayev and \uc2 Sberbank\uc2 's head German Gref (to April 9) MOSCOW- First Deputy Prime Minister Igor Shuvalov to meet with Russian business leaders MOSCOW- Slovenia's Foreign Minister Samuel Zbogar to hold talks with his Russian counterpart Sergei Lavrov MOSCOW- Palestinian President Mahmoud Abbas to visit Russia SAMARA/TOLYATTI, Russia- French Junior Trade Minister Anne-Marie Idrac to visit Russia (to April 9) YEKATERINBURG, Russia- Italian Economic Development Minister Claudio Scajola and Russia's Industry Minister Viktor Khristenko to participate in Russian-Italian economic forum MOSCOW- Russia's Agriculture Minister Yelena Skrynnik and Economy Minister Elvira Nabiullina to address the State Duma, lower house of parliament, on the agriculture reform MOSCOW- A government committee on Sakhalin-1 gas and oil project to hold a meeting MOSCOW- Fuel energy forum (to April 11). LINK: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://iprr.ru/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://iprr.ru/}}}\par \par \uc2 IN THE PAPERS [PRESS/RU]:\par \par \uc2 Vedomosti and Kommersant report that mobile phone sales fell 29 percent year-on-year in the first quarter as Russians tighten their belts in the face of the first recession in a decade.\par \par \uc2 Kommersant also reports that indebted car maker GAZ plans to cut around 4,000 staff by mid-year.\par \par \uc2 TOP STORIES IN RUSSIA AND THE CIS [RU-NEWS]: TOP NEWS: Moldovan police take control of president office [ID:nL7493305] Russia steps up gas pressure on Ukraine [ID:nnL7629506] Russia, Italy cement ties with new energy deals [ID:nL7407475] COMPANIES/MARKETS: Alfa suggests uniting \uc2 Vimpelcom\uc2 , Kyivstar -media [ID:nL8148914] Sistema sells Moscow developer stake for under $2[ID:nL7101067] Russia's \uc2 AvtoVAZ\uc2  agrees 8 bln rbl state loans [ID:nL0945055] EARNINGS POLL-Comstar Q4 net seen down 16 pct [ID:nL7970147] Sibir files $328 mln claim against ex-directors [ID:nL7380603] Russia \uc2 Gazprom\uc2  to launch dollar Eurobond-source[ID:nL7547526] Russia \uc2 Gazpromneft\uc2  places 5 bln rouble bond [ID:nL7411098] \uc2 Boeing\uc2  to help Russian Airlines on credit [ID:nL7948766] ECONOMY/POLITICS: Kremlin aide: IMF should study global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  [ID:nL7933144] Russia Jan-Feb trade surplus $15.3 bln-customs [ID:nL6453824] Russia corporate debt down by $30 bln in Q1 [ID:nL769593] ANALYSIS-Moldova riots have deep political roots[ID:nSHC764775] Jailed tycoon challenges Medvedev in court [ID:nL7570430] ENERGY: LUKOIL Q4 net loss $1.6 bln, misses forecast [ID:nL713280] Berlin see role for Rus