\par\par \b \uc2 FACTBOX-Key moves in Russian rouble\b0\par\par\uc2 1,105 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2009\par 11:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, March 26 (Reuters) - The Russian rouble is on track for record monthly gains versus the euro-dollar basket, in a sign that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has succeeded in putting a floor under devaluation expectations.\par \par \uc2 -- For an ANALYSIS on \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy see [ID:nLO388402].\par \par \uc2 Following are key facts on the rouble and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 BASKET <RUS=MCX>\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  introduced a euro/dollar basket for tracking the rouble's course on Feb. 1, 2005, initially made up of 0.1 euros and 0.9 dollars. The euro's share was gradually increased to reach the current 0.45 euros and 0.55 dollars composition on Feb. 8, 2007.\par \par \uc2 The basket's boundaries are now defined as 26 to 41 roubles, although officials have suggested they consider the more narrow 41-39 range more appropriate at current oil prices <URl-E>.\par \par \uc2 FOCUS\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  used investors' appetite for the rouble to allow a gradual appreciation as a means for fighting inflation until early August, when the trend reversed.\par \par \uc2 In the autumn 2008, authorities said their immediate focus had switched from fighting inflation to supporting the economy and markets through the global financial crisis and credit crunch.\par \par \uc2 On Nov. 11, 2008, Russia embarked on a controlled devaluation path, widening the rouble corridor in small steps.\par \par \uc2 From Jan. 23, authorities have sought to put an end to that process, defining the rouble's trading band. However the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has continued market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , occasionally buying or selling dollars to prevent excessive rouble volatility in either direction.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's First Deputy Chairman Alexei Ulyukayev on March 26 said the regulator has bought less than $5 billion on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market since the start of the month.\par \par \uc2 RESERVES\par \par \uc2 Russia's gold and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, the world's third largest, give it a powerful weapon against speculators betting on a weaker rouble, although the value of the cash pile has fallen by a third since early August.\par \par \uc2 The value of reserves has stabilised in the last two months along with the rouble. On March 20, they were $385.3 billion.\par \par \uc2 KEY ROUBLE MOVES\par \par \uc2 Jun. 26, 2007: appreciation of roughly 10 kopecks; \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's new bid level seen around 29.81 roubles\par \par \uc2 Aug. 8, 2007: appreciation of roughly 10 kopecks to 29.71\par \par \uc2 Aug. 9, 2007: appreciation of roughly five kopecks or 0.17 percent; \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's bid level seen at around 29.61 roubles\par \par \uc2 Jun. 10, 2008: appreciation of roughly 12 kopecks; \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's bid level established around 29.51 roubles\par \par \uc2 Jul. 9, 2008: appreciation of roughly 10 kopecks\par \par \uc2 Jul. 14, 2008: appreciation of roughly 15 kopeck\par \par \uc2 Jul. 15, 2008: brief appreciation to 29.28 roubles; dealers say \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's bid level seen at around 29.25 roubles\par \par \uc2 Aug. 4, 2008: appreciation to new high of 29.26 roubles, though \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's bid level is not breached\par \par \uc2 Aug. 8-11, 2008: rouble sells off sharply during Russia's military conflict with Georgia; \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sells an estimated $12-13 billion to stop basket weakening beyond 30.10.\par \par \uc2 Sep. 4, 2008: having let rouble weaken beyond 30.10 on Sep. 3, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  steps in to defend 30.40-41; it continues to defend that level with regular \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in following weeks.\par \par \uc2 Nov. 11, 2008: rouble is allowed to weaken, stabilising around 30.70-71, with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  saying it has widened the trading corridor by 30 kopecks in each direction; move comes a day after \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chairman Sergei Ignatyev said he did not rule out more flexibility in the exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 Nov. 24, 2008: \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  widens corridor again by 30 kopecks in each direction, allowing the rouble to weaken to 31\par \par \uc2 Nov. 28, 2008: another band widening, rouble eases to 31.33\par \par \uc2 Dec. 5, 2008: rouble weakens 31.63 a day after Prime Minister Vladimir Putin ruled out sharp \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate moves but said the rouble will fluctuate with commodity prices [ID:nPUTIN2]\par \par \uc2 Dec. 11, 2008: the band is widened to around 31.90\par \par \uc2 Dec. 15, 2008: the rouble weakens to around 32.20\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Dec. 17, 2008: the rouble weakens further by 45 kopecks --\par compared to 30 kopecks during the previous six moves -- to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 around 32.65, seen as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's new support level.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dec. 18, 2008: the rouble weakens to around 33.11, the first time devaluations occurred on two consecutive days\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dec. 22, 2008: the rouble weakens to around 33.45\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dec. 24, 2008: the rouble weakens as far as 33.79\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dec. 26, 2008: the rouble weakens to 34.31, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's first deputy chairman Alexei Ulyukayev says the regulator is sticking to gradual depreciation path, plans no one-off moves\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dec. 29, 2008: the rouble weakens to around 34.80\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Jan. 11, 2009: the rouble weakens to 35.30 on the first trading day of the year\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Jan. 12, 2009: the rouble weakens to 35.77\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Jan. 14, 2009: the rouble weakens to 36.30\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Jan. 15, 2009: the rouble weakens to 36.80 against the basket, confirming that depreciations are happening faster than in late December; rouble sinks to record low versus the dollar\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Jan. 16, 2009: the rouble weakens to 37.30\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Jan. 19, 2009: the rouble weakens to 37.80 as daily devaluations look set to become the norm\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Jan. 20-21, 2009: c.bank source says band widened again, but rouble rebounds, in part due to strong demand for cash to meet tax payments, strengthening as far as 36.56\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Jan. 22, 2009: c.bank announced that it will stop widening the corridor and set the upper basket boundary at 41 roubles.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Feb. 5, 2009: rouble briefly hits the 41 band boundary but recovers without any \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ; the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stabilises in the 41-39 range in subsequent weeks\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 March 20, 2009: rouble strengthens beyond 39 per basket; the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for four trading days in a row, dealer say, buying dollars and gradually moving its bid in 5 kopeck intervals to as far as 38.60.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 OUTLOOK\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  says it not planning to change the upper boundary for the basket in the coming months.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The 2009 government budget is based on an average dollar rate of 35.1 roubles, implying a basket rate of 41.42 roubles.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 One-year non-deliverable forwards (NDFs) show the dollar at 38.18 roubles, compared to 43.12 in mid-February <RUBNDF=GFI>.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Compiled by Toni Vorobyova and Gleb Bryanski; editing by Patrick Graham)\f28 \par \par \uc2 RUSSIA-ROUBLE/ (FACTBOX)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090326e53q001e0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
