\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Russia c.bank buys USD for 3rd day, oil at $50\b0\par\par\uc2 431 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2009\par 15:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds quotes, details, background)\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, March 23 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for a third consecutive trading day on Monday to slow down rouble appreciation, dealers said, as oil surged to $50 for the first time since November.\par \par \uc2 The rouble has been on an appreciation path in recent days thanks to stronger oil prices, buoyant domestic stock markets and some signs of bottoming out in economic data.\par \par \uc2 Russia's main oil export blend, Urals, rose to $50 a barrel <URL-E> and domestic stock indexes also hit 4-1/2-month highs.\par \par \uc2 The rouble recovery comes after it lost around a third of its value in six months to adjust for the worst economic outlook in a decade, with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spending tens of billions of dollars to keep \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  depreciation gradual.\par \par \uc2 The rouble firmed as far as 38.61 versus a euro-dollar basket, its strongest in nearly two months, before closing at 38.72 <RUS=MCX>.\par \par \uc2 "Now we may have an offload of long positions (in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) ... People were selling foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in order to buy (Russian shares)," said a dealer at a foreign bank, estimating official \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  at $1.5 billion.\par \par \uc2 Alexander Panasenko, dealer at Metallinvestbank, said the regulator likely bought around $1.0-1.5 billion.\par \par \uc2 Another boon for the rouble is Russian tax payments, with Trust Bank analyst Evgeny Nadorshin estimating that around 80 billion roubles ($2.40 billion) is due this week in total.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has pledged to keep the rouble within a 26-41 range versus the basket, but has also said it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent excessive volatility. Officials have indicated that they see current exchange rate levels as appropriate given the present price of key export oil.\par \par \uc2 "We view this level as a soft boundary, which authorities would only allow the rouble to appreciate beyond were oil prices to rise well above $50, giving rouble appreciation a fundamental justification," ING said in a research note.\par \par \uc2 "Without a recovery in oil prices, expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to firmly defend the 39 level, helping to restock the nation's \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves and preserve the benefits of weaker rouble." Russia's gold and \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, the world's third-largest, stood at $376 billion on March 13, down from a peak of nearly $600 billion last August. (Reporting by Andrei Ostroukh, writing by Toni Vorobyova; Editing by Andy Bruce)\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA-ROUBLE/ (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090323e53n0014i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
