\par\par \b \uc2 Belarus receives $500 mln tranche of Russian loan\b0\par\par\uc2 293 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2009\par 16:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 MINSK, March 12 (Reuters) - Belarus has received a $500 million tranche of a Russian loan agreed on last year and the money will go towards boosting foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Belarus last year received $1 billion of the $2 billion loan. It also received $788 million of a $2.5 billion IMF loan in January, and on Wednesday it agreed to a three-year \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap with China worth 20 billion yuan ($2.93 billion).\par \par \uc2 Most of the export-driven economy of the ex-Soviet state is still in state hands. Exports have dropped as the economic crisis grips Europe and the Belarussian rouble has been under pressure. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support it.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also considering lending up to 100 billion Russian roubles ($2.85 billion) which Belarus would use to transfer all accounts between the two countries into the Russian rouble.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rose in February to $3.8 billion from $3.4 billion, thanks to $625 million received from Russia's gas export monopoly \uc2 Gazprom\uc2  as payment for 12.5 percent of the Belarussian pipeline network.\par \par \uc2 Economic growth slowed in January-February to 1.4 percent from 9.9 percent in the first two months of last year. Inflation accelerated to 5.4 percent in the first two months against 3.2 percent a year ago.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  devalued the rouble by 20 percent on New Year's Day, as part of the loan agreement with the IMF. The rouble's rate was 2,880 to the dollar on Thursday. (Reporting by Andrei Makhovsky; Editing by Victoria Main)\par \par \uc2 BELARUS-RUSSIA/LOAN|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090312e53c001g9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
