\par\par \b \uc2 POLL-Weak rouble to bring Russian recovery in Q4\b0\par\par\uc2 618 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Februar 2009\par 12:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  * Analysts expect growth of 0.2 percent in Q4\par \par \uc2  * Economy expected to contract by 2.5 pct in 2009\par \par \uc2  * Forecasts vary widely, one sees 10 pct contraction in 2009\par \par \uc2  By Gleb Bryanski and Olga Borodina\par \par \uc2  MOSCOW, Feb 27 (Reuters) - The Russian economy will contract throughout 2009 but may show the first signs of growth in the fourth quarter due to devaluation of the rouble \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a poll of 14 economists showed on Friday.\par \par \uc2  The economy is expected to contract by 2.5 percent, close to the government's official forecast of 2.2 percent, but analysts expected growth of 0.2 percent in the final quarter, median forecasts showed.\par \par \uc2  "The policy of gradual devaluation of the rouble should bring results in 6-9 months through substitution of imports in food processing, manufacturing and construction," said Yelena Sharipova from Renaissance Capital.\par \par \uc2  Sharipova said she expected 3.3 percent growth in the fourth quarter and said higher oil prices towards the end of the year as well as comparatively weak growth in the fourth quarter of 2008 would also contribute. [ID:nLR652870]\par \par \uc2  However, the forecasts varied significantly and some projections were much gloomier. \par \par \uc2  "The economic contraction will soon get a new kick from a sharp fall in consumer demand and investment," said Igor Nikolayev from FBK, who forecast a 10 percent contraction for the year including a 7.0 percent slump in the fourth quarter.\par \par \uc2  Imports account for about one half of Russia's domestic demand but questions remain regarding how quickly Russian industry, starved of external credit and faced with prohibitive domestic interest rates, can turn around as it did after the 1998 crisis.\par \par \uc2  WAY OUT\par \par \uc2  The rouble <RUB=> lost one fourth of its value during 10 weeks of gradual devaluation from November to January when banks, firms and households changed their cash for foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Banks currently hold about $80 billion in their accounts.  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has vowed to defend the rouble at a level of 41 roubles to a basket made up of 0.55 dollars and 0.45 euros, provided that the oil price does not fall to $30 per barrel and stay there for some time. \par \par \uc2  Economists agreed that the regulator will be able to defend the 41 level in the short-term but by the end of the year the rouble will breach the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's defences and weaken further to 41.55 against the basket. \par \par \uc2  Economists saw Russia's gold and \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, still the world's third largest, falling to $337 billion by the end of the year from the current $391.9 billion, suggesting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue to support the rouble through \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Economists said \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy of large budget deficit, managed exchange rate, high interest rates and tight market liquidity will complicate the economic recovery but their views on a possible policy response varied. \par \par \uc2  Maxim Oreshkin from Rosbank said Russia should move over to an inflation targeting regime and float the rouble.\par \par \uc2  "The way out of the current situation would be a cut in the budget deficit to 3-4 percent of the gross domestic product and a transition to inflation targeting with a target of 5-7 percent inflation," he said.\par \par \uc2  Nikolai Kashcheyev from MDM said the government could chose instead to go back to exchange and capital controls, abandoned in 2006.\par \par \uc2  "An economic recovery is now possible only with the recovery in global demand or if the Russian economy is partially closed ... which would allow a stimulating economic policy," he said.  (Reporting by Gleb Bryanski and Olga Borodina; Editing by Jason Neely)  \par \par \uc2 RUSSIA-ECONOMY/POLL|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090302e52r001ka\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
