\par\par \b \uc2 Russian  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Buys Dollars To Cap Ruble Rise - Banker\b0\par\par\uc2 124 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Februar 2009\par 16:26\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Friday, buying dollars to prevent the ruble climbing too steeply after a week of record gains, a Moscow-based banker told Dow Jones Newswires.\par \par \uc2 "It spent millions of dollars (worth of rubles), not billions," the banker said.\par \par \uc2 The ruble closed Friday's session around flat at RUB39.09 against a basket of dollars and euros. It added almost 5% on the week as a whole.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't comment on its \b \highlight22\uc2 forex interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Web site: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.cbr.ru"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.cbr.ru}}}\par \par \uc2 -By Andrew Langley, Dow Jones Newswires; +7 495 937 8445; andrew.langley@dowjones.com [ 13-02-09 1526GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020090213e52d0010p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
