\par\par \b \uc2 =DJ FOCUS: No End In Sight For CEE  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Declines\b0\par\par\uc2 By Edith Balazs and Christopher Emsden OF DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 1,145 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Februar 2009\par 08:10\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2009, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BUDAPEST (Dow Jones)--Central Europe could be on the brink of a region-wide \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis.\par \par \uc2 Sharp drops of as much as 30% in the value of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Hungary, Poland, the Czech Republic, Romania and Russia in the past few months are a clear sign of the risk that broad-brush contagion may defy remedies tailored to fit specific countries.\par \par \uc2 Regional economies have seen manufacturing plummet as export markets and domestic credit flows dry up, carry trades unwinding and foreign capital fleeing nearly all asset classes.\par \par \uc2 'We do not, worryingly, sense that we are at the bottom just yet,' said Timothy Ash, head of emerging-markets research at \uc2 Royal Bank of Scotland\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The prospect of a swift and devastating chain reaction should a single country buckle under strong selling pressure is looming, and European policy makers cannot hide their heads in the sand, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 'There're a series of ticking time bombs like Romania, Bulgaria or Russia,' said Daniel Bebessy, analyst at Budapest Alapkezelo, a unit of GE Money. 'The domino effect in case of a crisis is beyond doubt,' he said.\par \par \uc2 The main eastern European Union \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are likely to fall another 10% to 15% by summer, analysts at Paris-based Natixis said.\par \par \uc2 Fundamentals are dreadful, with huge current account deficits now exposed to collapsing demand and sliding commodity prices, steering countries to the edge of an abyss.\par \par \uc2 'With poor or no growth prospects, shrinking foreign direct investment and fleeing portfolio investment, current account deficits become a liability,' said ING economist Agata Urbanska. Even \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  drops of 20% aren't enough to offset the pace of decline in exports, she said.\par \par \uc2 'We have, anyway, probably moved already beyond the realm of fundamentals,' said Gabor Ambrus, an economist at 4castweb in London. 'It is the realm of psychology guiding markets here, and the psychology is quite straightforward: these (\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) crosses will go up and will go up loads before we can retrace and fundamentals can again take control.'\par \par \uc2 While some of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  slides merely reverse the appreciation of recent years, when abundant credit made emerging economies a favorite investment destination, further falls might represent a dangerous overshooting making conventional monetary or fiscal policy tools largely ineffective while raising the cost of direct \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.\par \par \uc2 Both \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Kazakhstan have had to abandon their defense of managed \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pegs in the wake of severe depletion of their \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  drops are creating new frontiers of credit risk for lenders, said a senior bank executive at one of the euro-zone banks active in the region.\par \par \uc2 That's spreading across economies that should, under normal circumstances, present very different risk profiles, said the banker, who predicted extreme volatility over the next six months.\par \par \uc2 Indeed, among the worst performers are those the banker said ought to be the strongest, such as the Polish zloty, down 24% against the euro since September, and the Turkish lira, down 37% against the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 Poland and Turkey have better fundamentals and stronger banking systems than some other countries in the region but, in an environment driven by pessimism and fear, this seems hardly to matter. The situation already smells of contagion.\par \par \uc2 Skepticism about one \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the region can be transferred to others. Indeed, investors may be targeting more liquid \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , such as the Polish zloty or the Hungarian forint, as proxies for harder-to-trade risks such as the Bulgarian lev - which is pegged to the euro through a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board - or local banks, said ING's Urbanska.\par \par \uc2 'Let's face it...this is a medium-level domino effect,' said Martin Blum, chief analyst at \uc2 Unicredit\uc2  in Vienna. 'Whether it will evolve into a super-domino scenario depends on how far the International Monetary Fund is prepared to go.'\par \par \uc2 The IMF has so far organized emergency loans for Hungary, Latvia, Ukraine and Serbia. It is in talks with Turkey, and may soon negotiate aid packages with Poland, Romania and Bulgaria.\par \par \uc2 U.K. Prime Minister Gordon Brown, Monday, called for the IMF to do more to mitigate the risk of a regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  meltdown by providing funds to recapitalize banks in the region. The IMF has already let it be known it would like to double its reserves to $500 billion.\par \par \uc2 Unfortunately, 'investor worries remain unabated' even after the first round of IMF packages, Eurobank EFG said in a research note.\par \par \uc2 Nor has help from the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , offered to Hungary and Poland in the form of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps, been an effective panacea.\par \par \uc2 'Local banks are surviving on the ECB's life support of overnight liquidity facilities,' said Gyorgy Barcza, analyst at K&H Bank in Budapest, a unit of KBC. 'Should this be terminated, the problem would be enormous,' he said.\par \par \uc2 The ECB liquidity facilities were intended to be temporary to deal with a liquidity squeeze. They are, however, becoming part of the structural landscape. There is also the possibility that, should things get worse, the banks might need more swaps with the ECB, which might or might not provide them.\par \par \uc2 A full-blown \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis could hammer local banking systems, possibly even prompting euro-zone banks to abandon their franchises in the region, either through nationaliztion or, in a worst-case scenario, bankruptcy.\par \par \uc2 Such an outcome would be a brutal blow to integrated markets in the European Union. Policy makers are, therefore, under pressure to consider innovative measures to avoid such a scenario from happening.\par \par \uc2 Such solutions might entail the ECB offering more \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps to E.U. members outside the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  union, or even accepting government bonds from non-euro members as collateral so as to tangibly ease liquidity pressures and inject a strong vote of confidence into moody markets.\par \par \uc2 The ECB accepts euro-zone debt but has been reluctant to accept debt from outside the zone because of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  risk involved. But accepting such collateral could possibly reduce that very risk. This would be a big step for the bank but it is being mulled.\par \par \uc2 'It's essential to secure the backing of the ECB and wealthier euro-zone countries,' said Michal Dybula, an economist at \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2  in Warsaw. 'The reversal of capital flows (from these countries) could lead to an extremely prolonged recession,' he said. -By Christopher Emsden, Dow Jones Newswires; +39-02-58-21-99-05; chris.emsden@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 Click here to go to Dow Jones NewsPlus, a web front page of today's most important business and market news, analysis and commentary: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.djnewsplus.com/access/al?rnd=D2EWjHqyyCMxXzaj9fWW2g%3D%3D"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.djnewsplus.com/access/al?rnd=D2EWjHqyyCMxXzaj9fWW2g%3D%3D}}}\uc2 . You can use this link on the day this article is published and the following day.\par \par \uc2 -0-\par \par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2009 \uc2 Dow Jones & Company, Inc\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020090211e52b0040h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
