\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Russia hikes rates to support rouble, as promised\b0\par\par\uc2 By Toni Vorobyova and Dmitry Sergeyev   \par \uc2 739 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Februar 2009\par 09:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds data on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , inflation, updates prices)\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Feb 9 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will hike most interest rates by 100 basis points from Feb. 10, it said on Monday, fulfilling a promise to tighten monetary policy to support the rouble which reacted with modest gains.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials have said interest rates will be part of the arsenal used to ensure the rouble does not weaken beyond the 41 level against its euro-dollar basket, identified as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  floor after over two months of gradual devaluation to adjust to weak oil prices and the worst economic outlook in a decade.\par \par \uc2 Using interest rates to support the rouble should counter inflation, a major problem fuelled by the devaluation, as well as helping Russia preserve some of its reserves after spending over a third of the cash pile, or some $200 billion, over the past six months to avoid a 1998-style \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  collapse.\par \par \uc2 The minimum rate at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's one day repo auctions -- a key source of banking sector liquidity -- will be raised to 10.00 percent from 9.00 percent, the bank said on Monday.\par \par \uc2 The intent is to "contain inflationary tendencies and ensure the stability of the exchange rate of the rouble," it said.\par \par \uc2 Rates for a range of other \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  will also be hiked. The only ones unaffected were the rouble \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap rate, the refinancing rate and rates linked to the refinancing rate.\par \par \uc2 The rouble closed 0.4 percent stronger at 40.71 versus the basket <RUS=MCX>. It has touched the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 41 trading band boundary just once, briefly, last Thursday.\par \par \uc2 "It (the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) promised and it hiked ... It seems it does not really trust the (\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) speculators who have retreated a little, it thinks they may go on the attack again," said Nikolai Kashcheyev, analyst at \uc2 MDM Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "God willing, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will pass along the thin bridge between economic slowdown and rouble stability."\par \par \uc2 PRICE SURGE\par \par \uc2 Russia is heading for its first recession in a decade this year and lower rates could help support the economy.\par \par \uc2 But analysts say rate cuts will have to wait until the rouble has stabilised -- something that will be more easy to achieve with tighter monetary policy.\par \par \uc2 Inflation is also a big problem, despite easing global price pressures. Russian news agency Interfax reported on Monday that the Economy Ministry expects consumer prices to rise 3.8 to 4.0 percent in the first two months of this year, compared with a 3.6 percent increase in the same period of 2007 [ID:nL9212150].\par \par \uc2 By raising interest rates for its key liquidity \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hopes to discourage commercial banks from borrowing roubles and instead to prompt them to exchange some of their dollar and euro holdings into roubles.\par \par \uc2 "We expect the deficit of rouble liquidity to ease further pressure on the rouble in the near future. As a result, we reiterate our belief that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be able ... to defend the 41/basket support level, at least in the near future," \uc2 Unicredit\uc2  analysts said in a research note.\par \par \uc2 In January the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it has sold a net $34.2 billion and 4.1 billion euros [ID:nL9150493], although dealers say there were no \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the first week of February.\par \par \uc2 For their part commercial banks, such as state-controlled \uc2 Sberbank\uc2  have been raising rates on rouble savings accounts and cutting them on foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ones.\par \par \uc2 Higher rates may help lure back foreign investors who fled Russia in droves following a summer war with Georgia and the subsequent deepening of the global financial crisis. Russian rates compare favourably with U.S. rates of as low as zero, UK at 1 percent and euro zone at 2 percent [INT/RATE].\par \par \uc2 Russia last hiked rates a week ago, but at that time left the key minimum repo rate unchanged at 9 percent. Nonetheless the average rate at the daily auctions has been above 10 percent since Jan. 30. At Monday's second auction -- the last before the new minimum rate comes into effect -- they hit 10.92 percent.\par \par \uc2 -- For a TABLE of Russian interest rates see [ID:nL9229782] (Writing by Toni Vorobyova; Editing by Ruth Pitchford)\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA-RATES/ (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|G|RNP|PGE   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090209e5290011k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
