\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Russia stays out of market, warns against rouble bets\b0\par\par\uc2 By Oksana Kobzeva   \par \uc2 587 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Februar 2009\par 15:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds details, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  comments)\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Feb 6 (Reuters) - The Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  warned bankers against betting on any further rouble weakness on Friday, at the end of a week when for the first time in months it did not have to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  has allowed the rouble to lose a quarter of its value versus a euro-dollar basket in three months, gradually adjusting to low oil prices and the worst economic outlook in a decade.\par \par \uc2 Two weeks ago the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sought to put a floor under the rouble, vowing to stop it from weakening beyond 41 to the basket. But the epic battle forecast by market players has so far not materialised -- the rouble has stayed within the band, only touching it once briefly on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Investors are growing increasingly convinced that the regulator means business -- and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chairman Sergei Ignatyev reinforced that message at an annual meeting with bankers in a hotel near Moscow on Friday.\par \par \uc2 "41 roubles -- that is serious and for a long time. And people who are counting on playing on devaluation will be disappointed. An appreciation of the rouble is not out of the question," Ignatyev told some 300 bankers, according to one conference participant who added: "Ignatyev was brimming with confidence."\par \par \uc2 Keeping the rouble depreciation gradual has cost Russia a third of its reserves, or some $200 billion, and prompted its first sovereign rating downgrades in a decade.\par \par \uc2 But the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  gave Russian companies and citizens time to convert their savings into foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and helped to avoid public panic in a country that still remembers a 70 percent rouble collapse in 1998.\par \par \uc2 TIGHT REIN ON MARKET Dealers said they had seen no significant \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  this week, yet the rouble held within the band, closing on Friday at 40.86 to the basket.\par \par \uc2 The regulator had sold dollars each week since it began to gradually widen the rouble's trading band three months ago. The one exception was a week in January when it sold roubles to meet demand from corporates who had to pay taxes.\par \par \uc2 Now the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has other tools to try and support the rouble. By raising interest rates and reducing the amount of roubles it lends to the banking system, it hopes to prompt banks to convert their dollars and euros back into roubles.\par \par \uc2 "If necessary, (the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  promised to) cut the amount of collateral-free loans for banks, to raise interest rates on them," said another banker who attended the meeting, which was organised by an association of Russian regional banks.\par \par \uc2 His comments appeared to echo those of other \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials. Sergei Shvetsov, head of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's financial markets \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  department, said on Thursday that he did not think the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would have to defend the band "to the last drop of blood", and flagged the possibility of rate hikes.\par \par \uc2 "We think that this stabilisation (of the rouble) might prove much more sustainable than previous support levels, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  seems to have started to limit liquidity injections into the market, which should eventually undermine the speculative run on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and provide support to the rouble," \uc2 Unicredit\uc2  said in a research note. (Additional reporting by Andrei Ostroukh and Toni Vorobyova; Editing by Ruth Pitchford)\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA-ROUBLE/ (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|BNX|G|RNP|DNP|PTD|PGE|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090206e526001yy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
