\par\par \b \uc2 =DJ 2nd UPDATE:  \highlight22\uc2 Russia \highlight\uc2  Ends Devaluation; \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  To Continue\b0\par\par\uc2 609 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Januar 2009\par 19:06\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2009, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    (Recasts with a new lead, official quotes, detail, background.) \par  \par    By Andrew Langley and Lidia Kelly \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MOSCOW (Dow Jones)--Russia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Thursday it was halting its gradual devaluation of the ruble but said it will continue \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market to ensure the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's stability.\f28 \par \par \uc2 In an unusual departure from its deliberately vague ruble management policy of past months, Chairman Sergei Ignatyev said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will set the upper limit of the Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's trading band at 41 rubles against a basket of 55% dollars and 45% euros, weaker than the 39.2 rubles set previously.\par \par \uc2 "The actual level of the ruble may be significantly (stronger) than this," Ignatyev said at a press conference.\par \par \uc2 The bank's move seems to be directed at Russian banks, which have been increasingly speculating that the dollar will rise against the ruble. Renaissance Capital investment bank in Moscow values the banks' speculative positions in recent weeks at $50 billion.\par \par \uc2 Ignatyev said there is "enough foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  liquidity" in the banking system.\par \par \uc2 "Banks can sell their foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  assets to receive rubles," he said.\par \par \uc2 As a result of the managed depreciation, which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  instigated in mid-November, the ruble has shed a quarter of its value. Ignatyev said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has enough reserves for now to ensure the new limit won't be breached. In addition, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's money-lending policy will ensure the ruble's stability by controlling liquidity levels more closely.\par \par \uc2 And when needed, the bank will step in, Ignatyev said.\par \par \uc2 "We will keep \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  not only at the trading band limits, but also inside the corridor to stabilize the ruble and prevent any drastic fluctuations," he added.\par \par \uc2 Russia has spent billions of dollars in reserves to cushion and slow the ruble's weakening in the last three months amid plummeting oil prices and an exodus of foreign capital.\par \par \uc2 Officials insist a one-off devaluation would have sent shock waves through the population at large, possibly sparking a run on ruble deposits, and would also have wreaked havoc on businesses which have instead had time to slowly adjust.\par \par \uc2 Many Russians remain wary of keeping savings in rubles after the 1998 financial crisis wiped out many bank deposits, and officials have consistently reassured citizens there will be no sharp drops again.\par \par \uc2 But as the gradual devaluation policy became clear, it encouraged many to place bets on further weakening, putting downward pressure on the Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is hoping to inject much higher two-way ruble volatility, deterring speculators from betting on steady further ruble weakening," analysts at \uc2 RBC Capital Markets\uc2  said in a note. "The current approach has (also) become much too costly in terms of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserve loss."\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday said reserves dipped below $400 billion during the last week. While they remain the world's third-biggest stockpile, they have now dropped by $200 billion since last August and some have said more erosion could throw Russia's sovereign investment-grade rating into question.\par \par \uc2 This week has seen pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ease as companies that had previously been hoarding dollars and euros scooped up rubles to cover monthly tax payments and responded to the Kremlin warning that devaluation is drawing to a close.\par \par \uc2 The ruble closed Thursday at RUB37.03 against the basket. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Web site: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.cbr.ru"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.cbr.ru}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Andrew Langley and Lidia Kelly, Dow Jones Newswires; +7 495 937 8445; andrew.langley@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 January 22, 2009 13:06 ET (18:06 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020090819e51m0o93h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
