\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Russia \highlight\uc2 's Ignatyev: Will Continue To  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  In Ruble Trade\b0\par\par\uc2 132 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Januar 2009\par 17:21\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in ruble trading, despite concluding its gradual devaluation of the national \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chairman Sergei Ignatyev said Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Ignatyev told reporters the bank would act to prevent sharp fluctuations in the ruble by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  both at the extremities of its managed trading range and within the corridor itself.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday said it would set the upper boundary of the trading corridor within which it manages the ruble exchange rate at RUB41 to a basket of 55% U.S. dollars and 45% euros.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  site: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.cbr.ru"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.cbr.ru}}}\par \par \uc2 -By Lidia Kelly, Dow Jones Newswires; +7 495 937 8445; lidia.kelly@dowjones.com [ 22-01-09 1641GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020090122e51m000qi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
