\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3-Russia seeks to end run on rouble\b0\par\par\uc2 880 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Januar 2009\par 08:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds Ignatyev comments, details, quotes)\par \par \uc2 * Russia seeks to set floor for rouble\par \par \uc2 * c.bank says will continue \b \highlight22\uc2 FX interventions\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  set for 1st recession in decade\par \par \uc2 By Gleb Bryanski and Yelena Fabrichnaya\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Jan 22 (Reuters) - Russia sought to put a limit on the rouble's two-month slide on Thursday, setting a floor 10 percent below current levels in a bid to see off speculators after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stabilised in recent sessions.\par \par \uc2 The statement ended a two-month long period of creeping devaluation as Russia strove to bring the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in line with weak oil prices and an economy which the government expects to slip into its first recession in a decade this year.\par \par \uc2 Moscow has spent $200 billion, or a third of its reserves, since August on making the rouble's fall a gradual one, seeking to avoid panic among a population mindful of a 70 percent \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  collapse during the 1998 crisis.\par \par \uc2 Analysts say Prime Minister Vladimir Putin's chances of returning to the Kremlin in 2012 hinge on the handling of the current turmoil, which has knocked nearly a fifth off the rouble and sent Russian stock markets to multi-year lows.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would stop widening the rouble trading corridor from Jan. 23, setting the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's boundaries at between 26 and 41 versus a basket of 0.45 euros and 0.55 dollars. The rouble closed at 37.03 <RUS=MCX>, aided by a deadline for company tax payments, which are paid in roubles. "The stated value is defined taking into account the remaining risks of worsening terms of trade for the Russian Federation," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 "But the Bank of Russia sees these risks as moderate and does not plan to change this boundary in the coming months."\par \par \uc2 The bank still has an arsenal of around $400 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to back up the range and the rouble has already shown signs of resilience, accompanied by official signals that the depreciation could be nearing an end.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  posted its biggest ever rally versus the basket, and has held firm since then despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announcing further corridor widenings on Wednesday and Thursday.\par \par \uc2 "It is a sensible move. They had been very keen to avoid a sudden devaluation for political reasons so we have this instead," said Nigel Rendell, emerging \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Royal Bank of Canadain London.\par \par \uc2 "A lot of people have been short on the rouble for a long time and they might decide the game is up and close their positions so there might be some short-term support. But the longer-term trend is clearly down unless we get some kind of inversion in the oil price."\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief Sergey Ignatyev told a press conference that the regulator would continue to smooth out the rouble's path, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  both at the boundaries and in between, and the decision took into account risks of speculative attack.\par \par \uc2 WATCHING OIL\par \par \uc2 The stabilisation of the rouble came as Russian companies faced heavy demand for cash this week to meet domestic tax payments, and some analysts were sceptical that the upbeat mood on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would last.\par \par \uc2 "This is likely just to build in expectations of more to come, and yet more capital flight. It probably buys the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  some time, but that's about it," said Timothy Ash, analyst at RBS in London.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has argued that the softly-softly approach to devaluation has avoided the sort of panic rush to change savings into dollars that followed the rouble's slide in 1998.\par \par \uc2 Putin this week ordered that the 2009 budget be reworked at an average price of $41 for the country's key oil exports -- less than half the originally forecast $95 -- and the result is expected to be a budget deficit of around 8.5 percent of GDP.\par \par \uc2 Revised economy ministry forecasts obtained by Reuters showed gross domestic product will fall 0.2 percent this year.\par \par \uc2 Falling imports -- as the economy slows -- will likely keep the trade balance in surplus, supporting the rouble. But some say even the $41 oil assumption -- based on current prices of Russia's Urals export blend -- is optimistic.\par \par \uc2 Ignatyev said changes in the oil price could prompt a rethink on the rouble boundaries. "If the oil price falls to $30 per barrel and stays there, it is possible but not necessary that we will have to adjust the (upper) boundary," he said.\par \par \uc2 A cheaper rouble makes life easier for Russia's commodity exporters who have a rouble cost base but dollar earnings. But it is a tough pill to swallow for importers and for companies who have large foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  debts to pay back.\par \par \uc2 -- For an INSTANT VIEW on Thursday's news see [ID:nLM12578]\par \par \uc2 -- For a FACTBOX on rouble moves see [ID:nRUBFACTS] (Additional reporting by Vlasta Demyanenko, Katya Golubkova in Moscow and Peter Apps in London; writing by Toni Vorobyova; Editing by Ruth Pitchford and Patrick Graham)\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA-ROUBLE/(UPDATE 3)|LANGEN|C|D|E|M|O|U|MTL|GRO|SOF|OIL|G|RBN|AFA|CSA|LBY|RWSA|RWS|REULB|GNS|ABX|BNX|FUN|RNP|PGE   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090122e51m000k7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
