\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3-Rouble firm, devaluation course still unclear\b0\par\par\uc2 By Yelena Fabrichnaya and Andrei Ostroukh   \par \uc2 713 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Januar 2009\par 08:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds c.bank \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Jan 21 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rouble held onto gains on Wednesday after Tuesday's big rally, but analysts attributed the strength to demand for cash to pay taxes and said it was too soon to call an end to months of devaluation.\par \par \uc2 The rouble has lost around a fifth of its value versus a euro-dollar basket since November when Russia began a creeping devaluation process to reflect the fall in oil prices and the worst economic outlook in a decade.\par \par \uc2 Up until Tuesday, keeping the depreciation gradual was costing Russia billions of dollars a day, taking its reserves down to $426.5 billion from almost $600 billion in August.\par \par \uc2 This week provided the first signs that the depreciation -- which has scared Russians into shifting money into dollars and euros, stunted the domestic bond market and hit companies' balance sheets -- could soon be over.\par \par \uc2 Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought between $4 billion and $5 billion in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Wednesday and was likely to continue \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases for the rest of the week.\par \par \uc2 However, analysts are still far from sure about whether the rouble has found a floor, and about the bigger question of how fast Russia is prepared to move towards its stated medium term goal of a free-floating \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The rouble strengthened as far as 36.56 versus the euro-dollar basket on Wednesday <RUS=MCX>, before stabilising around 37.30 -- holding on to Tuesday's gains of 1.3 percent, its biggest jump since Russia set the current composition of the basket at 0.55 dollars and 0.45 euros two years ago.\par \par \uc2 The rouble recovery prompted the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to enter the market with dollar sales for the first time in months, dealers said, in a bid to avoid overly sharp \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves.\par \par \uc2 Kremlin's top economic aide Arkady Dvorkovich on Tuesday said the bulk of the weakening was nearing its end and Finance Minister Alexei Kudrin forecast medium-term rouble gains.\par \par \uc2 Analysts remained cautious however, attributing much of this week's bounce to the need for roubles to meet tax payments.\par \par \uc2 "Of course it is a signal to those who were playing against the rouble that the trend is not that predictable," said Stanislav Ponomarenko, head of Russia research at ING.\par \par \uc2 "But it is too soon to say that this is the exact level at which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will hold the rouble. This is linked to temporary factors, the shortage of roubles for tax payments. We will only be able to talk about a pause in two weeks."\par \par \uc2 There was also a bit of cheer from the market on the economic front, with data showing the number of people affected by wage arrears halved to 300,000 in December [ID:nLL91382].\par \par \uc2 BYE BYE BASKET?\par \par \uc2 UniCredit\uc2  estimated that Russian companies must pay around 300 billion roubles in taxes by Jan. 28.\par \par \uc2 To help meet demand, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  allocated a record 559 billion roubles ($17 billion) in Wednesday's first repo auction and for the second day has set no limit on its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  -- another key source of liquidity.\par \par \uc2 The rouble rebound came even as a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said the regulator had widened the rouble's trading band on both Tuesday and Wednesday -- moves which up until now resulted in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's immediate retreat to the new weaker boundary.\par \par \uc2 "It's possible this is a signal that they are going to change policy," said Julia Tsepliaeva, chief economist for Russia and CIS at \uc2 Merrill Lynch\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The widening of the band is reminiscent of an abandonment of the bi-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket ... (when) there is no commitment to keep the exchange rate stable against the basket."\par \par \uc2 Such a move could be a step in the direction of a free float of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  -- a policy which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is aiming for in the medium term as part of its move to targeting inflation rather than the exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 -- For a FACTBOX on rouble moves see [ID:nRUBFACTS] (Reporting by Yelena Fabrichnaya, Andrey Ostroukh and Toni Vorobyova)\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA-ROUBLE/ (UPDATE 3)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090121e51l000uh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
