\par\par \b \uc2 Russia spent $7-8 bln defending rouble Thurs-dealers\b0\par\par\uc2 160 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Januar 2009\par 15:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Jan 15 (Reuters) - Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent between $7 billion and $8 billion defending the rouble at new, weaker levels on Thursday after allowing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sink to record lows versus the euro and the dollar, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 The rouble closed at 36.82 versus a euro-dollar basket on Thursday, after Russia staged the fourth mini-devaluation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the last five days <RUS=MCX>.\par \par \uc2 "There is no longer the question of when they will do it (devalue), it is clear that this will happen," said Vitaly Andreyev at Nomos Bank, estimating the day's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  at around $8 billion.\par \par \uc2 A dealer at another Russian bank estimated $7.5 billion, while one at a foreign bank said $7 billion. (Reporting by Andrey Ostroukh, writing by Toni Vorobyova; editing by Maria Kiselyova)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 RUSSIA\b0 \highlight\uc2 -ROUBLE/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTIONS\b0 \highlight\uc2  (URGENT)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090115e51f001fl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
