\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Russia \highlight\uc2  pauses on gradual rouble devaluation path\b0\par\par\uc2 580 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Januar 2009\par 08:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , background, quotes)\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Jan 13 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent around $3 billion defending the rouble on Tuesday after two days of mini-devaluations, dealers estimated, suggesting it does not want to let the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decline gather pace.\par \par \uc2 Moscow started devaluing the rouble just over two months ago in response to falling oil prices, prospects of an economic recession and widespread capital flight from emerging markets.\par \par \uc2 Returning from long new year public holidays, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  delivered two more mini-devaluations before pausing on Tuesday, keeping a similar pace to late December when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was allowed to weaken six times in the last 10 trading days.\par \par \uc2 "They are keeping up the speed," said Julia Tsepliaeva, chief economist for Russia and the CIS at \uc2 Merrill Lynch\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "For the process (of devaluations) to stop ... capital flight must end, the population must believe in the rouble and stop converting their savings from roubles into foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 The rouble closed at 35.79 versus the euro-dollar basket which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  uses to guide the exchange rate <RUS=MCX>, around the level seen as the new \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  support after Monday's devaluation.\par \par \uc2 In the first minutes of trade it briefly weakened as far as 36 to the basket, but quickly recovered, with dealers saying the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had stepped into the market with dollar sales.\par \par \uc2 "It is possible the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had not yet had time to put in its offer (when the rouble briefly fell to 36)," said Stanislav Yarushevichus, head of trading at ING in Moscow.\par \par \uc2 "It seems the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is present in the market today, there is a pause in the weakening. But we have not yet reached the level which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  finds acceptable; another 7-10 percent (depreciation) is possible in the next month."\par \par \uc2 Some analysts say a big one-off move would make more sense than gradual depreciation. But officials from \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chiefs to Prime Minister Vladimir Putin have publicly ruled out a sharp devaluation.\par \par \uc2 Another possible reason for Tuesday's pause in the devaluations could be the euro's weakening to a one-month low against the dollar. <EUR=> [FRX/]\par \par \uc2 Remembering the 1998 financial crisis, when the rouble lost around 70 percent of its value, Russians been shifting money into euros and dollars.\par \par \uc2 With most Russians watching the rouble's rate versus the dollar, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has tended to coincide the devaluations with bouts of euro strength, so that the brunt of the move is borne by the euro/rouble rate while dollar/rouble moves less.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, the rouble hit a new 6-year low of 31.29 to the dollar <RUB=>, but edged up versus the weaker euro <EURRUB=>.\par \par \uc2 Against the basket, the rouble is now around 18 percent below historic peaks set in early August. Since then the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has spent around a quarter of Russia's gold and \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves on defending the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and smoothing out its depreciation path. The cash pile is now under $440 billion.\par \par \uc2 Dealers estimated Tuesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  at $3 billion after $8 billion on Monday.\par \par \uc2 "These are our reserves which are being spent, which are melting. It shows that this policy of gradual steps is a costly one," said Tsepliaeva at Merrill. (Reporting by Andrey Ostroukh and Toni Vorobyova; Editing by Ruth Pitchford)\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA-ROUBLE/ (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|G|RNP|PGE   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090113e51d000ga\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
