\par\par \b \uc2 FACTBOX-Key moves in Russian rouble exchange rate\b0\par\par\uc2 884 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Dezember 2008\par 10:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Dec 24 (Reuters) - The Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  widened the rouble trading band for the seventh time in December on Wednesday, and for the 10th time since it embarked on a path of controlled \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  devaluation in mid-November.\par \par \uc2 The rouble has now lost more than 15 percent versus the euro-dollar basket from its historic peak, set just before a war with Georgia in August combined with a global rout in emerging markets to trigger capital flight from Russia.\par \par \uc2 -- For a story on Wednesday's move see [ID:nLO184082]\par \par \uc2 Following are key facts on the rouble and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 BASKET <RUS=MCX>\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  introduced a euro/dollar basket for tracking the rouble's course on Feb. 1, 2005, initially made up of 0.1 euros and 0.9 dollars. The euro's share was gradually increased to reach the current 0.45 euros and 0.55 dollars composition on Feb. 8, 2007.\par \par \uc2 The widening of the band has taken the rouble to its weakest level versus the basket since its current composition was set.\par \par \uc2 FOCUS\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  used keen investor appetite for the rouble to allow gradual appreciation as a means of fighting inflation until early August, when the trend reversed.\par \par \uc2 Authorities have now said their immediate focus has switched from fighting inflation to supporting Russia's economy and markets through the global financial crisis and credit crunch.\par \par \uc2 RESERVES\par \par \uc2 Russia's gold and \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, the world's third largest, give it a powerful weapon against speculators betting on a weaker rouble.\par \par \uc2 But the value of the cash pile has fallen by over a quarter since early August, to stand at $435.4 billion on Dec. 12.\par \par \uc2 Analysts have said such rapid decreases in reserves are dangerous, especially given weaker oil prices that slow inflows of new money and potentially signal demands on reserves from future years' budgets.\par \par \uc2 Standard & Poor's\uc2  on Dec. 8 became the first ratings agency to downgrade Russia in a decade.\par \par \uc2 KEY ROUBLE MOVES\par \par \uc2 Jun. 26, 2007: appreciation of roughly 10 kopecks; \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's new bid level seen around 29.81 roubles\par \par \uc2 Aug. 8, 2007: appreciation of roughly 10 kopecks to 29.71\par \par \uc2 Aug. 9, 2007: appreciation of roughly five kopecks or 0.17 percent; \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's bid level seen at around 29.61 roubles\par \par \uc2 Jun. 10, 2008: appreciation of roughly 12 kopecks; \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's bid level established around 29.51 roubles\par \par \uc2 Jul. 9, 2008: appreciation of roughly 10 kopecks\par \par \uc2 Jul. 14, 2008: appreciation of roughly 15 kopeck\par \par \uc2 Jul. 15, 2008: brief appreciation to 29.28 roubles; dealers say \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's bid level seen at around 29.25 roubles\par \par \uc2 Aug. 4, 2008: appreciation to new high of 29.26 roubles, though \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's bid level is not breached\par \par \uc2 Aug. 8-11, 2008: rouble sells off sharply during Russia's military conflict with Georgia; \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sells an estimated $12-13 billion to stop basket weakening beyond 30.10.\par \par \uc2 Sep. 4, 2008: having let rouble weaken beyond 30.10 on Sep. 3, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  steps in to defend 30.40-41; it continues to defend that level with regular \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in following weeks.\par \par \uc2 Nov. 11, 2008: rouble is allowed to weaken, stabilising around 30.70-71, with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  saying it has widened the trading corridor by 30 kopecks in each direction; move comes a day after \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chairman Sergei Ignatyev said he did not rule out more flexibility in the exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 Nov. 24, 2008: \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  widens corridor again by 30 kopecks in each direction, allowing the rouble to weaken to 31\par \par \uc2 Nov. 28, 2008: another band widening, rouble eases to 31.33\par \par \uc2 Dec. 5, 2008: rouble weakens 31.63 a day after Prime Minister Vladimir Putin ruled out sharp \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate moves but said the rouble will fluctuate with commodity prices [ID:nPUTIN2]\par \par \uc2 Dec. 11, 2008: the band is widened to around 31.90\par \par \uc2 Dec. 15, 2008: the rouble weakens to around 32.20\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Dec. 17, 2008: the rouble weakens further by 45 kopecks --\par compared to 30 kopecks during the previous six moves -- to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 around 32.65, seen as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's new support level. Dec. 18, 2008: the rouble weakens to around 33.11, the first time devaluations occurred on two consecutive days\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dec. 22, 2008: the rouble weakens to around 33.45\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dec. 24, 2008: the rouble weakens as far as 33.79\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 OUTLOOK\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Further rouble weakness is expected, with some analysts saying a large one-off move will eventually be unavoidable, though others reckon the current pace of devaluations is fast enough to have a good chance of being effective.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The median forecast in a Reuters poll [ID:nRUPOLL] published on Dec. 23 showed the rouble at 36.24 versus the basket and 31.01 versus the dollar <RUB=> by end-2009.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Economy Ministry's 2009 dollar/rouble forecasts and euro/dollar assumptions [ID:nLH190875] suggest the rouble will be in the 34-36 range versus the basket next year.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 One-year non-deliverable forwards (NDFs) show the rouble at around 35 to the dollar <RUBNDF=GFI>. (Compiled by Toni Vorobyova and Gleb Bryanski; editing by Tony Austin)\f28 \par \par \uc2 RUSSIA-ROUBLE/ (FACTBOX)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020081224e4co000fj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
