\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3-Russia devalues rouble for sixth time, more to come\b0\par\par\uc2 By Gleb Bryanski   \par \uc2 681 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Dezember 2008\par 08:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds c.bank \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Dec 22 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  devalued the rouble for the sixth time this month on Monday and financial markets are convinced more is in store as it bids to right an economy stricken by the financial crisis and falling oil prices.\par \par \uc2 The bank has allowed markets to knock almost 14 percent off the rouble since an Aug. 4 peak and 9 percent since Nov. 11, when it began a series of mini-devaluations to protect its dwindling foreign reserves and bolster economic growth.\par \par \uc2 A source at the bank said on Monday it had widened the trading band again, allowing the rouble to weaken by another 30 kopecks to 33.45 against the dollar/euro basket <RUS=MCX>.\par \par \uc2 Some dealers said the nomination of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's chief trader for a board position on Monday also suggested it was happy with policy so far and could continue a drive to a weaker rouble -- making exports more competitive going forward.\par \par \uc2 "The market is in such a state that it expects another devaluation every day," said \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer Mikhail Spolokhov from Nomos bank.\par \par \uc2 The rouble has depreciated as far in the past month as economists had expected it to weaken during the whole of next year -- in a Reuters poll in late November, the end-2009 forecast had been 33.44, end-2008 was 31.30.\par \par \uc2 "We are pleased to see the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  accelerating the devaluation, and expect to see more such moves before the end of the year," Pharos Financial Group fund managers said in a daily market comment.\par \par \uc2 Analysts view the rouble exchange rate as still undervalued even after the devaluations and traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent between $2.0 and $2.5 billion supporting the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Time is running out for the bank to make more moves, with markets closing for a long New Year and Orthodox Christmas holiday between Dec. 31 and Jan. 11.\par \par \uc2 BRAIN AND SOUL\par \par \uc2 On Monday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also recommended its chief trader Sergei Shvetsov, 37, who oversees \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  as well as management of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gold and \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, to become a new board member.\par \par \uc2 Shvetsov, who joined the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 1993, has kept a low public profile as head of an open market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  department that has kept financial markets guessing on policy throughout the global crisis.\par \par \uc2 "We all know that Shvetsov is a soul and brain of the Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. He was always an intellectual driver of the exchange rate policy and therefore unlikely this policy will change," said Alexei Moiseyev from Renaissance Capital.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  runs a managed float of the rouble, keeping it stable against the basket, made up of 0.55 dollars and 0.45 euros. The rouble closely follows the price of oil, Russia's main export commodity.\par \par \uc2 STICK AND CARROT\par \par \uc2 Some of the devaluation moves have coincided with dollar weakness, masking the change for the general public which focuses on the dollar/rouble rate <RUB=>.\par \par \uc2 A weaker dollar also masks the decline in Russia's gold and \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, still the world's third largest at $435.4 billion.\par \par \uc2 Even so, the rouble stood near three-year lows against the dollar while fresh trade balance data suggested imports were already hit by the weak rouble.\par \par \uc2 Interfax news agency said Russia's trade surplus shrank to $7.1 billion in November, the smallest surplus since at least January 2005. Imports were flat year-on-year, while exports slumped by 27 percent, it said.\par \par \uc2 Officials say they have got \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculation under control compared with previous months when Russian and foreign banks bet on the rouble's weakening and opened long foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions. For a FACTBOX on key rouble moves [ID:nROUBLEFAC] (Additional reporting by Andrei Ostroukh; editing by Tony Austin/Patrick Graham)\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA-ROUBLE/ (UPDATE 3)|LANGEN|C|D|E|M|O|U|MTL|GRO|SOF|OIL|G|RBN|ABX|BNX|FUN|RNP|PGE   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020081222e4cm000ez\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
