\par\par \b \uc2 Fitch Downgrades ROOF Russia S.A.\b0\par\par\uc2 581 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Dezember 2008\par 12:45\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Fitch Ratings-Moscow/London-19 December 2008: Fitch Ratings today downgraded all tranches issued by ROOF Russia S.A., removed the Rating Watch Negative (RWN) and assigned a Negative Outlook to all ratings as follows:\par \par \uc2 Class A (ISIN XS0298206193): Downgraded to 'BBB-' (BBB minus) from 'A-' (A minus); Outlook Negative\par \par \uc2 Class B (ISIN XS0298206946): Downgraded to 'BB+' from 'BBB'; Outlook Negative\par \par \uc2 Class C (ISIN XS0298208058): Downgraded to 'BB-' (BB minus) from 'BB'; Outlook Negative\par \par \uc2 Class D (ISIN XS0298208991): Downgraded to 'B-' (B minus) from 'B'; Outlook Negative\par \par \uc2 The downgrade resolves the Rating Watch Negative assigned to the ratings on 13 November 2008. It is driven by the lasting pressure on Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  versus the US dollar. In Fitch's view the continued devaluation will have a detrimental effect on the portfolio's performance.\par \par \uc2 Since August 2008 the rouble has lost 15% of its value versus the US dollar. This continuously increases the liability of borrowers under the USD denominated loans securitised via ROOF Russia S.A.. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  (CBR) has in the past heavily \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend a foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime that links the rouble to a foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket consisting of USD and EUR. However, in recent weeks the trading band was broadened in small steps eight times until today. If further and more severe depreciation is allowed, the pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be directly passed on to the underlying debtors. As such the indirect protection borrowers benefited from previously, continues to fade away.\par \par \uc2 The increasing debt burden of borrowers under the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  loans can trigger two scenarios that are of concern to Fitch. Firstly, the default frequency of debtors will increase due to the household's income falling short of the rising payment obligation. To take this risk into account, Fitch has revisited its default rate assumptions attached to the various ratings levels.\par \par \uc2 Secondly, rising pressure on the borrowers could prompt the authorities to re-denominate USD debt into local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Depending on the conversion rate used and the subsequent exchange rate movements, such \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could lead to collections falling short of their expected amounts in USD terms. The transaction has no structural protection against this risk.\par \par \uc2 The transaction is scheduled to remain revolving until May 2010 and the available credit protection for the notes has only changed slightly since closing. As such the credit enhancement structure falls short of supporting Fitch's revised assumptions at their current rating levels.\par \par \uc2 These two aspects drive today's rating action. The Outlook on the ratings remains Negative reflecting Fitch's view that the performance of the portfolio is vulnerable to rapid deterioration in the coming months.\par \par \uc2 The transaction is a securitisation of auto loan receivables originated by ZAO Raiffeisenbank (rated 'A-'(A minus), Negative Outlook). Its current outstanding balance amounts to USD398m.\par \par \uc2 Contact: Michael Hoelter, Moscow, Tel: +7 495 956 9946; Jaime Sanz London, +44 (0) 207 682 7279.\par \par \uc2 Media Relations: Julian Dennison, London, Tel: +44 020 7682 7480, Email: julian.dennison@fitchratings.com.\par \par \uc2 Fitch's rating definitions and the terms of use of such ratings are available on the agency's public site, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.fitchratings.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.fitchratings.com}}}\uc2 . Published ratings, criteria and methodologies are available from this site, at all times. Fitch's code of conduct, confidentiality, conflicts of interest, affiliate firewall, compliance and other relevant policies and procedures are also available from the 'Code of Conduct' section of this site. [ 19-12-08 1147GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020081219e4cj000ff\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
