\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Russia defends rouble as more devaluations seen\b0\par\par\uc2 423 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Dezember 2008\par 15:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds quotes, background)\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Dec 16 (Reuters) - Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent around $5 billion supporting the rouble on Tuesday, dealers said, adding that the exchange rate was pressured by expectations of further devaluations in coming days.\par \par \uc2 Faced with weak oil prices, worsening economic fundamentals and broad capital flight from emerging markets, Russia has allowed six mini-devaluations of the rouble in the past five weeks. The most recent move happened on Monday [ID:nLF619070]. The rouble closed at 32.20 versus a euro-dollar basket <RUS=MCX>, around the level seen as current \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  support.\par \par \uc2 "It looks like today they bought a fiver from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said a dealer at a Russian bank, referring to billions of dollars. Others confirmed his estimate.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the rouble have helped slash \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gold and \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves by a quarter since early August, to under $440 billion, galvanising authorities into the gradual depreciation policy starting in mid-November.\par \par \uc2 A darkening economic backdrop is adding to pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with industrial output slumping at its fastest rate in a decade, while wage arrears doubled in November [ID:nLG197439].\par \par \uc2 "The weakness of the industrial economy plus the lower oil price reinforces the case for further rouble depreciation, either in steady small steps, as seen in recent weeks, or a one-off adjustment of 10-20 percent in early 2009," RBC analysts said in a research note.\par \par \uc2 Russians have started to shift their money into foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and authorities, keen to avoid panic, have repeatedly stressed there will be no sharp moves in the exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 Most of the depreciations have been timed to coincide with broad-based dollar weakness. That means the brunt of the depreciation versus a euro-dollar basket is borne by the euro. The dollar/rouble rate -- more closely watched by ordinary Russians -- remains relatively stable <RUB=>.\par \par \uc2 The dollar hit a two-month low against the euro on Tuesday <EUR=>, fanning talk of another weakening of the rouble soon.\par \par \uc2 "Euro/dollar is continuing to rise and it has been noted that such a backdrop is convenient for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  if it wants to widen the trading boundaries," said Alexei Zaitsev, dealer at \uc2 UniCredit\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "It seems (market participants) are expecting that tomorrow the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will take advantage of this opportunity."\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Andrey Ostroukh, writing by Toni Vorobyova; editing by Patrick Graham)\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA-ROUBLE/ (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020081216e4cg001cz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
