\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3- \highlight22\uc2 Russia \highlight\uc2  c.bank devalues rouble as reserves shrink\b0\par\par\uc2 804 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Dezember 2008\par 08:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , percentage moves, closing level)\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  allows 5th rouble devaluation in a month\par \par \uc2 * Reserves down $17.9 billion in latest week\par \par \uc2 * Analysts say weak data may speed up depreciation\par \par \uc2 By Yelena Fabrichnaya and Toni Vorobyova\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Dec 11 (Reuters) - The Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  allowed the fifth one percent devaluation in the rouble against the dollar/euro basket in a month on Thursday as fresh data showed a $17.9 billion drop in gold and \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves last week.\par \par \uc2 The rouble weakened as far 31.89 from 31.63 against the basket, made of 0.55 dollars and 0.45 euros, at the start of the trading session. It closed at 31.84. The rouble is down 8.3 percent against from historic peaks set in early August.\par \par \uc2 The reserves fell to $437.0 billion on Dec. 5 from their peak of $597.5 billion on Aug. 8 when Russia sent tanks to Georgia, triggering a wave of capital flight. Since then the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been selling dollars to support the rouble.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday dealers said the regulator did not need to sell dollars to defend the new support level as investors bought roubles on expectation there will be no more moves this week.\par \par \uc2 A source at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed the regulator had widened the rouble's trading band to the basket, used to guide the exchange rate policy. In an environment of low oil prices and capital outflows such widening leads to a weaker rouble.\par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Alexei Kudrin told reporters he fully backed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy while the bank's Chairman Sergei Ignatyev declined to comment. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has kept a low profile since the start of the depreciation in November.\par \par \uc2 The move followed the release of the third quarter GDP data which showed the growth slowing to a three-year low. Analysts have said that with the price of oil also at three-year low, the gradual depreciation policy was not working.\par \par \uc2 "If \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserve depletion continues at the current rate, and oil prices fail to rally, the Russian authorities are likely to undertake a more aggressive, one-off move to weaken the rouble," said Timothy Ash from \uc2 Royal Bank of Scotland\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 SPEED UP WIDENING\par \par \uc2 Ash argued such move may come around a 10-day New Year and Orthodox Christmas holiday next month when banks will be closed, which will help avoid a run on deposits in commercial banks.\par \par \uc2 Russian officials including Prime Minister Vladimir Putin have said there will be no sharp fluctuations of the rouble.\par \par \uc2 A stable \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is viewed as one of the most significant achievements of Putin's eight years as president. But officials admit the rouble must adjust to lower oil prices.\par \par \uc2 "This quarter and the next quarter the authorities will see how badly the economy is hurt and that should, if anything, speed up the depreciation," said Citi analyst Elina Ribakova said. A weaker rouble should boost economic growth.\par \par \uc2 Russia aims to fully float the rouble within three years as part of transition to inflation targeting regime.\par \par \uc2 "In our view, it would make sense to speed up the widening of the trading band and let the market help find a reasonable level for the rouble, thus avoiding draining \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves excessively," said Lars Rasmussen at \uc2 Danske Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is taking advantage of a euro at a six-week high versus the dollar, which makes the devaluation moves against the basket less obvious for the general public, who closely watch the rouble/dollar rate.\par \par \uc2 Thus, while the rouble has weakened by a total of around 5 percent versus the basket since devaluations started exactly a month ago, it has lost only 2 percent against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Volumes on dollar/rouble deals with tomorrow's settlement reached $7 billion on the MICEX exchange, with some traders suggesting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could have used strong rouble demand to replenish its dwindling \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves.\par \par \uc2 "I think the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is buying back what it sold yesterday (when \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  were estimated around $5 billion), because without the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  it would be very hard to get such high volumes," said a dealer at a major foreign bank.\par \par \uc2 Standard & Poor's\uc2  this week became the first agency to downgrade Russia in a decade, but the sovereign has no immediate eurobond issue plans and officials have shrugged off the news.\par \par \uc2 The reserves, made of 45 percent dollars, 44 percent euros 10 percent pounds and one percent yen, also fall when the dollar strengthens against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which took about $5-6 billion off the reserves last week, according to analysts. (Additional reporting by Andrei Ostroukh; writing by Gleb Bryanski; Editing by Andy Bruce)\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA/ROUBLE (UPDATE 3)|LANGEN|ABX|BNX|FUN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020081211e4cb000oq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
