\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Russia gets first rating downgrade in 10 yrs\b0\par\par\uc2 808 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Dezember 2008\par 13:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  (Adds finance ministry reaction, quote, \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 ; cuts)\par \par \uc2  * \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's S&P rating cut to two notches above junk\par \par \uc2  * Pressure on reserves from oil, rouble\par \par \uc2  * S&P decision expected, market reaction muted\par \par \uc2  MOSCOW/LONDON, Dec 8 (Reuters) - \uc2 Standard & Poor's\uc2  on Monday became the first ratings agency to downgrade Russia in a decade, while data showed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had spent $30 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  last month.\par \par \uc2  S&P said it was keeping a negative outlook on Russia's new BBB foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rating and BBB+ long-term rouble rating.\par \par \uc2  "The negative outlook reflects the likelihood of a (further) downgrade if the banking crisis and external pressures continue to impair the government's balance sheet and its still substantial arsenal of liquid assets, amid a weakening of underlying economic fundamentals," it said in a statement.\par \par \uc2  S&P, which has had Russia on negative outlook since Oct. 23, was the last of the three global ratings agencies to promote Russia to investment grade after Moscow got its house back in order following the 1998 financial crisis.\par \par \uc2  "It is like a notification to the Russian Finance Ministry, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the government that even if there is no risk of outright default by the federal government, the rating agencies are watching and that their respect for Russian economic management has fallen after recent events," said Anton Tabakh, fixed income analyst at Troika Dialog in Moscow.\par \par \uc2  A Finance Ministry official told Reuters the downgrade would limit borrowing opportunities for domestic debt issued next year, but should not hurt bond prices for now [ID:nL8160773].\par \par \uc2  Russia, which has not recently needed to use bonds to raise cash, stopped issues this year due to a lack of demand.\par \par \uc2  Investors have pulled back heavily from Russia since the August conflict with Georgia. Pressured by the global financial crisis and plummeting oil prices, Russia has been spending tens of billions of dollars to support its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the real economy and the financial markets.\par \par \uc2  Falling oil prices <URL-E> mean money may also be needed to prop up the budget.\par \par \uc2  The ratings decision "is linked to the fall in the oil price and the likely appearance of current account and trade deficits next year. The weakening of the rouble and the situation with the exchange rate could have also played a part," said Yaroslav Lissovolik, chief strategist at Deutsche bank in Moscow.\par \par \uc2  "To a certain extent markets were already discounting the probability of such an outcome, so it is a negative for markets but it probably won't have a big impact."\par \par \uc2  INVESTMENT GRADE INTACT\par \par \uc2  Russia's stock markets stayed near session highs after the downgrade, focusing more on the day's recovery in oil prices <.IRTS>. Benchmark five-year credit default swaps (CDS), used as insurance against a default, were also little changed at around 787 basis points compared to around 811 on Friday, traders said.\par \par \uc2  Russia's 2030 eurobond was yielding 11.61/49 <RU011428878=>.\par \par \uc2  The downgrade leaves Russia's bonds two notches above junk.\par \par \uc2  "There is no justification for a loss of investment grade unless reserves were to fall to about $150 billion," said Chris Weafer, analyst at UralSib in Moscow.\par \par \uc2  "We still assume that the government will bite the bullet and devalue long before getting anywhere close to that. Keeping the rouble stable is a clear current priority. Preserving the country's investment grade status is simply non negotiable. It is by far the number one priority. It has to be." The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold $30 billion last month [ID:nL5405161] and dealers estimated Monday's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  at $2 billion.\par \par \uc2  Over the past month it has allowed the rouble to weaken in four one-percent steps versus a euro-dollar basket <RUS=MCX> some analysts say a sharper move eventually is inevitable.\par \par \uc2  Public foreign debt stood at just $40.4 billion on Oct. 1 -- less than a 10th of Russia's gold and \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves. But banks and companies have borrowed freely in recent years, and are now appealing for state help in debt refinancing as the global credit crunch has effectively shut foreign credit sources.\par \par \uc2  S&P's rivals have Russia three notches into investment grade territory. Fitch rates it BBB+ with a negative outlook as of Nov. 10. \uc2 Moody's\uc2  has it at Baa1 with a positive outlook, unrevised since the summer.\par \par \uc2  -- For S&P's statement see [ID:nWLA3139]\par \par \uc2  -- For analysts' views on the downgrade see [ID:nL871647]  (Reporting by Yelena Fabrichnaya, Guy Faulconbridge, Dmitry Zhdannikov and Toni Vorobyova in Moscow, Peter Apps and Sebastian Tong in London; Editing by Andy Bruce/Ruth Pitchford)  \par \par \uc2 RUSSIA-S&P/ (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|C|D|E|M|O|U|MTL|GRO|SOF|OIL|G|RBN|RNP|PGE   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020081208e4c8000sv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
