\par\par \b \uc2 FACTBOX-Key moves in Russian rouble exchange rate\b0\par\par\uc2 680 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 November 2008\par 12:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  Nov 28 (Reuters) - Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  allowed the rouble to weaken for the third time in a month on Friday, with analysts saying the move confirmed it was on a gradual depreciation path.\par \par \uc2  The rouble has now lost around seven percent versus the basket from its historic peak, set just before a military conflict with Georgia in August combined with a global rout in emerging markets triggered capital flight from Russia.\par \par \uc2  -- For a story on Friday's move see [ID:nLS296410]\par \par \uc2  Following are key facts on the rouble and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  BASKET\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  introduced a euro/dollar basket for tracking the rouble's course on Feb. 1, 2005, initially made up of 0.1 euros and 0.9 dollars. The euro's share was gradually increased to reach the current 0.45 euros and 0.55 dollars composition on Feb. 8, 2007.\par \par \uc2  FOCUS\par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  used keen investor appetite for the rouble to allow gradual appreciation as a means of fighting inflation until early August, when the trend reversed, prompting it to switch from slowing appreciation to supporting the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  Authorities have now said their immediate focus has switched from fighting inflation to supporting Russia's economy and markets through the global financial crisis and credit crunch.\par \par \uc2  RESERVES\par \par \uc2  Russia's gold and \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, the world's third largest, give it a powerful weapon against speculators betting on a weaker rouble.\par \par \uc2  But the value of the cash pile has fallen by a quarter since early August, to stand at $449.9 billion on Nov. 21.\par \par \uc2  Analysts have said such rapid decreases in reserves are dangerous, especially given weaker oil prices that slow inflows of new money and potentially signal demands on reserves from future years' budgets.\par \par \uc2  KEY ROUBLE MOVES\par \par \uc2  Jun. 26, 2007: appreciation of roughly 10 kopecks or a third of a percent; traders say \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's bid level for basket established around 29.81 roubles\par \par \uc2  Aug. 8, 2007: appreciation of roughly 10 kopecks or a third of a percentage point to 29.71 roubles\par \par \uc2  Aug. 9, 2007: appreciation of roughly five kopecks or 0.17 percent; \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's bid level seen at around 29.61 roubles\par \par \uc2  Jun. 10, 2008: appreciation of roughly 12 kopecks, or a third of a percentage point; \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's bid level established around 29.51 roubles\par \par \uc2  Jul. 9, 2008: appreciation of roughly 10 kopecks or a third of a percentage point\par \par \uc2  Jul. 14, 2008: appreciation of roughly 15 kopecks or 0.48 percent\par \par \uc2  Jul. 15, 2008: brief appreciation to 29.28 roubles; dealers say \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's bid level seen at around 29.25 roubles\par \par \uc2  Aug. 4, 2008: appreciation to new high of 29.26 roubles, though \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's bid level is not breached\par \par \uc2  Aug. 8-11, 2008: rouble sells off sharply during Russia's military conflict with Georgia; \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sells an estimated $12-13 billion to stop basket weakening beyond 30.10.\par \par \uc2  Sep. 4, 2008: having let rouble weaken beyond 30.10 on Sep. 3, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  steps in to defend 30.40-41; dealers estimate it sold up to $4 billion. \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues to defend that level with regular \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in following weeks.\par \par \uc2  Nov. 11, 2008: rouble is allowed to weaken, stabilising around 30.70-71, with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  saying it has widened the trading corridor by 30 kopecks in each direction; move comes a day after \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chairman Sergei Ignatyev said he did not rule out more flexibility in the exchange rate and some rouble weakness was possible.\par \par \uc2  Nov. 24, 2008: rouble is allowed to weaken as far 31 to the basket, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  says had widened corridor by another 30 kopecks in each direction.\par \par \uc2  Nov. 28, 2008: rouble is allowed to weaken as far as 31.31 to the basket in a third 30-kopeck move in a month. Market participants say further gradual devaluation is likely.  (Writing by Toni Vorobyova; editing by Tony Austin)  \par \par \uc2 RUSSIA-ROUBLE (FACTBOX)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020081128e4bs000tp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
