\par\par \b \uc2 No c.bank rouble buying seen after band widened\b0\par\par\uc2 169 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 November 2008\par 15:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Nov 24 (Reuters) - Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not need to spend reserves to defend the rouble's new support level on Monday after allowing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken by one percent against a euro-dollar basket, dealers said. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  widened the rouble's trading band by 30 kopecks in either direction, allowing it to weaken to 31 roubles to the basket.\par \par \uc2 But the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  promptly recovered some losses as companies prepared for month-end tax payments and banks had to pay back maturing \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  loans. It closed at 30.87 <RUS=MCX>.\par \par \uc2 "We managed without the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Stanislav Yarushevichus, head of trading at ING in Moscow.\par \par \uc2 On the day of the previous band widening, on Nov. 11, Russia spent an estimated $7 billion defending the new support level. (Reporting by Andrei Ostroukh and Toni Vorobyova; Editing by Maria Kiselyova)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 RUSSIA\b0 \highlight\uc2 -ROUBLE/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTIONS\b0 \highlight\uc2  (URGENT)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020081124e4bo00143\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
