\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 4-Russia allows second rouble weakening in 2 weeks\b0\par\par\uc2 784 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 November 2008\par 08:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , GDP data)\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  allows second rouble weakening in two weeks\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakens 1 pct to as far as 31 vs basket\par \par \uc2 * C.bank says widens trading corridor by 30 kopecks each way\par \par \uc2 By Yelena Fabrichnaya and Toni Vorobyova\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Nov 24 (Reuters) - Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  allowed the rouble to weaken by one percent versus a euro-dollar basket for the second time in two weeks on Monday, in a move which is seen as part of a gradual depreciation policy.\par \par \uc2 The rouble has come under heavy pressure as the oil price collapses, investors flee emerging markets, and local companies and ordinary Russians start to shift some of their money into foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The worsening macroeconomic situation is another negative for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with data on Monday showing annual economic growth slowing to its weakest pace in a year in October and the Economy Ministry cutting its 2008 expansion forecast to 6.8 percent.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  -- which has admitted it spent $57.5 billion defending the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in September and October -- first allowed a one percent weakening on Nov. 11, letting the rouble slip past the previously-defended 30.41 level to around 30.71. On Monday, the rouble weakened as far as 31.01 <RUS=MCX>.\par \par \uc2 "It is a technical decision. We have allowed the widening of the corridor by 30 kopecks in each direction," an official at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's press office told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 With Russia's reserves down by over a fifth from their early August peaks and some of the cash earmarked for an economy rescue package, analysts had expected further devaluations.\par \par \uc2 Authorities' comments also seemed to leave the door open for a gradual rouble weakening, with Prime Minister Vladimir Putin and others focusing their rhetoric on ruling out sharp moves.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  ... has entered a phase of gradual devaluations. Today is not the last step," said Ulrich Leuchtmann, analyst at \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2  in Frankfurt.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will try to do it as slowly as possible but it's restricted by the fact that ... they are running out of ammunition to defend the rouble and at the same time the rouble remains under pressure."\par \par \uc2 TIGHT LIQUIDITY\par \par \uc2 The price of Russia's benchmark Urals crude has fallen to around $45 a barrel <URL-E> -- less than half the level factored into next year's budget and suggesting that there will be less oil money coming in to replenish reserves in the future.\par \par \uc2 Some analysts have said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could take advantage of any temporary dollar weakness to make a rouble/basket devaluation less worrying for ordinary Russians who tend to focus on the dollar/rouble rate <RUB=>.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, the dollar was down 1.9 percent against a basket of six major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  <.DXY>.\par \par \uc2 The maturing of nearly 400 billion roubles ($14 billion) of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  loans on Monday and month-end tax payments could also cap short-term pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , potentially making it an opportune time to announce a band widening.\par \par \uc2 The demand for roubles was illustrated by the surge in interbank money market rates, with one-, two-, three- and six-month Mosprime rates all at historic highs <MOSPRIME=>, as well as by the fact that the rouble retreated from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's new support level to close at 30.87.\par \par \uc2 Dealers said there were no evident \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the new level, in contrast to the last band widening, on the day of which authorities sold around $7 billion.\par \par \uc2 On that occasion, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  followed up the band widening by raising the key refinancing rate to 12 percent in a bid to increase the rouble's yield appeal. Analysts said another rate hike was possible this time.\par \par \uc2 Moscow's bourses <.MCX> showed little reaction to the weaker rouble, rising on the back of improved global risk appetite.\par \par \uc2 However some analysts question whether the gradual depreciation programme will work.\par \par \uc2 "It's not necessarily a good move because it will not defuse speculation on the need for further rouble depreciation," said Benoit Anne, EMEA \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  and debt strategist at \uc2 Merrill Lynch\uc2  in London, forecasting a 10 percent depreciation in the first half of 2009.\par \par \uc2 Russian officials on Monday estimated retail deposit outflows of around 6 percent from banks last month. Russians are taking money out of rouble accounts, and putting only part of it in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  deposits instead. (Additional reporting by Andrei Ostroukh; Writing by Toni Vorobyova; Editing by Ruth Pitchford and Victoria Main)\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA-ROUBLE/ (UPDATE 4)|LANGEN|C|D|E|M|O|U|MTL|GRO|SOF|OIL|BNX   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020081124e4bo000fz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
