\par\par \b \uc2 WRAPUP 1-Russia FinMin says mild rouble weakening right decision\b0\par\par\uc2 750 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 November 2008\par 15:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Russia \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent $57.5 bln in 2 months to prop rouble\par \par \uc2 * Finance minister defends allowing mild rouble weakening\par \par \uc2 * Russia has reduced holdings of U.S. mortgage agency debt\par \par \uc2 By Yelena Fabrichnaya and Gleb Bryanski\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Nov 19 (Reuters) - Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  admitted on Wednesday it had spent $57.5 billion in two months on supporting the rouble, and Finance Minister Alexei Kudrin said allowing a mild weakening was the right decision in such circumstances.\par \par \uc2 The rouble has come under heavy pressure as the oil price collapses, investors flee emerging markets and local companies as well as ordinary Russians start to shift some of their money into foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 With memories of the 1998 financial crisis and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  collapse still potent, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has ardently defended the rouble against a basket of 0.45 euros and 0.55 dollars.\par \par \uc2 The exercise has been a costly one -- \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Sergei Ignatyev said on Wednesday \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  had sold $57.5 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in September and October.\par \par \uc2 With dollars needed to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and also to fund part of Moscow's $200 billion rescue package for markets and the economy, Russia has been reducing its holdings of some foreign assets.\par \par \uc2 Ignatyev said its holdings of U.S. bond agencies' \uc2 Fannie Mae\uc2  and \uc2 Freddie Mac\uc2  debt had fallen to $20.9 billion on Nov. 1 from $65.6 billion at the start of the year, as maturing paper is not replaced. In mid-September, Russia held around $30 billion in the two agencies.\par \par \uc2 Latest figures show Russia's reserves, accumulated as oil prices surged to record highs, have fallen to $475 billion since reaching a peak of nearly $600 billion in August.\par \par \uc2 Analysts were increasingly saying such a drain could not continue and last week the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced a widening of the trading band by 30 kopecks in either direction, resulting in a one percent depreciation of the rouble <RUS=MCX>.\par \par \uc2 "We paid for the stability," Kudrin told the Duma lower house of parliament on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is carrying out a mild widening of the rouble corridor. This is normal, this will allow us to keep the exchange rate stable and to spend less reserves ... I support these moves of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , even though it is independent."\par \par \uc2 BILLIONS GONE\par \par \uc2 Economists, who had expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to start depreciating the rouble next year at the earliest, slammed the timing of the move, saying it threatened to destabilise banks and contradicted the government's official line.\par \par \uc2 Kudrin's statement suggested the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's action had full government backing. Officials maintain there will be no sharp exchange rate fluctuations.\par \par \uc2 Since allowing the depreciation, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has defended the rouble at around the 30.70 level, dealers say, though analysts reckon further weakening is likely to follow.\par \par \uc2 Despite spending reserves on \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  and having already contributed $14 billion to the government's bank bailout programme, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  seems to have kept the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  structure of reserves broadly unchanged.\par \par \uc2 Ignatyev said as of Nov. 1, reserves were 45 percent held in U.S. dollars, about 44 percent in euros, "just above" 1 percent in Japanese yen and 10 percent in British pounds. The figures are broadly in line with previously aired breakdowns.\par \par \uc2 Kudrin said he expected inflationary pressures to subside next year, with inflation rates falling to about 8 percent and creating room for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to start cutting official interest rates in the second half of 2009.\par \par \uc2 Kudrin said he did not see "uncontrolled" risks for the budget coming from some regions where authorities engaged in risky lending schemes. He said the budget will be reviewed in January-February to take into account regional financing needs.\par \par \uc2 About 18 percent of Russia's National Wealth Fund has already been invested in domestic stock and bonds, Kudrin said, adding this reflected changing priorities in Russia's oil wealth management. But his words fell on deaf ears.\par \par \uc2 "You robbed the country. Billions are gone with the wind. You invested money in the U.S. economy -- the main culprit behind the global crisis," ultra-nationalist deputy Vladimir Zhirinovsky told Kudrin at the Duma. (Reporting by Yelena Fabrichnaya and Gleb Bryanski, writing by Toni Vorobyova; Editing by Ruth Pitchford)\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA-ECONOMY/ (WRAPUP 1)|LANGEN|C|D|E|M|O|U|MTL|GRO|SOF|OIL|G|RBN|NAT|ABX|BNX|FUN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PGE   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020081119e4bj001dp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
