\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Russia sold $16 bln to support rbl this wk-dealers\b0\par\par\uc2 By Andrei Ostroukh   \par \uc2 450 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 November 2008\par 15:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds quotes, background)\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Nov 14 (Reuters) - Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold around $16 billion to support the rouble this week, according to dealers' estimates, despite allowing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken one percent versus the dollar-euro basket.\par \par \uc2 The rouble closed at 30.70 <RUS=MCX> versus the basket on Friday, around the level seen as the new \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  support. It broke through the previously defended 30.41 mark on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Tuesday saw the heaviest \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , estimated at $7 billion, as the devaluation took investors by surprise -- most had not expected it until next year.\par \par \uc2 The estimates suggest Russia's reserves are likely to post another hefty fall when this week's data is published next Thursday. Rouble-supporting \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  have already helped slash them by a fifth in the last three months [ID:nMOS005337].\par \par \uc2 "Judging by the (dollar) purchases, the market is expecting that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will take another devaluation step next week, may be of one percent," said a dealer at an international bank in Moscow.\par \par \uc2 The rouble has been hurt by capital flight from Russia, as falls in oil and stock prices and broad-based risk aversion weigh on sentiment already bruised by high-profile corporate wrangles and the summer war with Georgia.\par \par \uc2 There are also signs that Russians are growing less confident in the rouble, with banks seeing outflows from rouble deposits and inflows into foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ones.\par \par \uc2 "We believe that Russian households also rushed to buy hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the news that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had allowed the rouble to depreciate," VTB Capital said in a research note.\par \par \uc2 Faced with a weakening rouble, Russia has stepped up efforts to increase its use in international trade, though analysts doubt this will help in the short-term [ID:nLE523144].\par \par \uc2 Some are now predicting a devaluation of as much as 20 percent by the end of next year, although Kremlin's top economic aide Arkady Dvorkovich said on Thursday that such a large weakening of the rouble was possible only if oil prices <URL-E> weaken to $8 a barrel from $50 currently [ID:nLD541618].\par \par \uc2 Dealers said that in the very near term the rouble could get some support from tax payments due next week, though they doubted any boost would prove lasting.\par \par \uc2 "There is real demand for foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ...Banks do not want to take short positions in the rouble but their clients are asking for it," said Viktor Kholoshnoy, dealer at Gazprombank. (Reporting by Andrei Ostroukh, writing by Toni Vorobyova, editing by Victoria Main)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 RUSSIA\b0 \highlight\uc2 -ROUBLE/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTIONS\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020081114e4be001y0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
