\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3-Russia reserves drop past $500 bln as rescue takes off\b0\par\par\uc2 By Gleb Bryanski   \par \uc2 681 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Oktober 2008\par 08:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds c.bank instruction, analyst)\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Oct 30 (Reuters) - Russia's gold and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves fell below the $500 billion mark for the first time in eight months, data showed on Thursday, suggesting the Kremlin's cash is starting to flow into the economy.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showed reserves fell $31 billion in the week to Oct. 24 to stand at $484.7 billion. Traders told Reuters the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent only $13 billion propping up the rouble during the last week.\par \par \uc2 "A stunning one-week drop, more than twice the fall in the previous weeks," said Anna Zadornova from \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The rating agencies are closely watching Russia's reserves, which are dwindling as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  burns foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in daily market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Many analysts say such policy is unsustainable and \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  will soon devalue the rouble.\par \par \uc2 Credit ratings agency \uc2 Standard & Poor's\uc2 , which cut Russia's outlook to negative from stable last week, warning of the costs of bailing out troubled banks and a rising risk of a budget deficit, declined to comment.\par \par \uc2 "The drop in reserves corresponds to a potential drop in the total foreign debt, so I do not see a drama there," said Yevgeny Nadorshin, analyst at Trust Bank.\par \par \uc2 The euro, which accounts for about 40 percent of Russia's reserves, weakened by 6 percent against the dollar <EUR=>, which accounts for about 49 percent. Sterling, which makes up about 10 percent of reserves, also weakened versus the U.S. unit <GBP=>.\par \par \uc2 That also contributed to the fall of reserves, whose total value is calculated in dollars.\par \par \uc2 UNDER ATTACK FROM POPULATION\par \par \uc2 Russia also plans to use $50 billion of its reserves to help corporations redeem their foreign debt. \uc2 United Company RUSAL\uc2 , owned by Russia's richest man Oleg Deripaska, on Wednesday became the first beneficiary, securing a $4.5 billion loan.\par \par \uc2 The government has also disbursed around $3 billion to billionaire Mikhail Fridman's \uc2 Alfa Group\uc2  and state oil major Rosneft to help refinance their foreign debts.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  plans to transfer the cash in small tranches to state-owned VEB bank, also known as Development Bank, tasked with administering the package. Reuters sources said VEB's board approved loans worth a total of $7.9 billion.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has spent tens of billions of dollars of its reserves since August to prevent the rouble from weakening beyond the 30.41 level against a euro-dollar basket.\par \par \uc2 Several of the western banks investing in Russia said last week they expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  at some stage to allow the rouble to depreciate.\par \par \uc2 "We expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to continue to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the near term by defending the rouble in an effort to calm the population's fears ... and because it perceives itself to be under speculative attack from the markets," Goldman's Zadornova said.\par \par \uc2 From last week, the bank introduced daily limits on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a further bid to deter speculators from betting on a fall in the rouble. On Thursday, the day's swap limit was set at zero for the first time.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also told commercial banks to keep a lid on growth in their foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  denominated assets in a bid to stop \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculation and a flight from rouble deposits, which accelerated sharply in October.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  warned it will monitor the banks' compliance with the instruction and make decisions to grant individual banks collateral-free loans based on the results of the monitoring.\par \par \uc2 "We believe the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is mainly under attack by the Russian population," said Zadornova.\par \par \uc2 The rouble gained four kopecks versus the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket to trade at 30.34 by 1255 GMT <RUS=MCX>, possibly drawing some cheer from this week's resurgence on Moscow's bourses [.ME]. (Additional reporting by Toni Vorobyova and Yelena Fabrichnaya) (Reporting by Gleb Bryanski; Editing by Andy Bruce)\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA-RESERVES/ (UPDATE 3)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|G|RNP|PGE   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020081030e4au000yk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
