\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3-Russian reserves slump, S&P points to debt rating risk\b0\par\par\uc2 By Toni Vorobyova   \par \uc2 716 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Oktober 2008\par 09:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds Thursday's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  estimate, quote, Goldman)\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Oct 16 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves dropped $32.2 billion in the last two weeks, data on Thursday showed, and a ratings agency warned more falls could be bad news for the country's credit standing as it battles market turmoil.\par \par \uc2 Moscow has committed some of the cash pile it has accumulated from high oil and gas prices to propping up a banking system and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pummelled by a flight of investors amid the wider global ructions.\par \par \uc2 Reserves are now down $66.9 billion, or 11 percent, since early August, when the military conflict with Georgia accelerated the capital flight and prompted the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to step into the market to protect the rouble.\par \par \uc2 Reserves hit a near-six month low of $530.6 billion on Oct. 10, and dealers' estimates of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  showing most of the latest week's $15.5 billion fall came from the bank selling dollars to aid the rouble.\par \par \uc2 UniCredit\uc2  and Goldman both estimated last week's capital outflows at $13 billion, bringing their projections for outflows since early August to over $60 billion.\par \par \uc2 "The key anchor of Russia's rating has always been its buffers, the large reserves," S&P credit analyst Frank Gill said during a conference call.\par \par \uc2 "If we see those continue to haemorrhage, that would be the best forward indicator as to what the rating could do."\par \par \uc2 S&P cut the outlook on its BBB+ rating for Russia to stable from positive last month.\par \par \uc2 As well as \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the reserves have been depressed by falling oil <CLc1> and commodity prices -- which lead to lower tax revenues for the resource-focused economy -- and by fluctuations in the euro/dollar exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 Moscow has also committed $50 billion of the reserves for future use in its markets rescue package to help companies refinance foreign debts, plus a further 960 billion roubles ($36.74 billion) for subordinate loans to banks.\par \par \uc2 Gill said S&P was not against Russia using its oil wealth to stave off a crisis in the banking system.\par \par \uc2 "Our bigger concern in Russia is not using these funds necessarily but the administration -- how are they actually going to be distributed," he said.\par \par \uc2 "Will some of that money get lost in the shuffle, will some of it become part of the capital flight? That's our biggest concern, if some of the reserve funds ended up offshore."\par \par \uc2 TIME TO SHORT THE ROUBLE?\par \par \uc2 The rouble closed at 30.40 against a euro-dollar basket, around the level the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been defending. Dealers estimated the day's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  at around $4 billion, with some saying a vicious circle was forming.\par \par \uc2 "Roubles are leaving the system, but people don't need too many dollars, so they swap back (for roubles) at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Vitaliy Andreyev, dealer at Nomos Bank.\par \par \uc2 Russian share indexes lost over 10 percent at one point during the day, falling to levels not seen since mid-2005.\par \par \uc2 "Sharp declines of Russian equity and securities markets on the negative external and domestic newsflow are likely the primary reason for continued capital flight, which is expected to persist in the near future," \uc2 UniCredit\uc2  analyst Vladimir Osakovsky said in a note.\par \par \uc2 "The flipside of continued reserve loss is likely increasing focus on whether the CBR will hold the band."\par \par \uc2 One reason against allowing the rouble to weaken, analysts say, is that it could lead to public panic or even bank runs. But some reckon it cannot support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  forever.\par \par \uc2 "The amount of short term debt due in the two coming quarters will force the CBR to the let the RUB (rouble) go and we will be looking for levels to build a short RUB position against the basket," \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2  said in a research note.\par \par \uc2 -- For a table of reserves data, see [ID:MOS005327]\par \par \uc2 -- For a FACTBOX on the Russian economy see [ID:nLG232546]\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Toni Vorobyova and Andrey Ostroukh; editing by Patrick Graham and Victoria Main)\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA-RESERVES/ (UPDATE 3)|LANGEN|C|D|E|M|O|U|MTL|GRO|SOF|OIL|NAT|G|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PGE   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020081016e4ag000m8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
