\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Emerging Markets-Rout continues, Iceland untraded\b0\par\par\uc2 769 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Oktober 2008\par 12:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (adds wider debt spreads, Romania \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 * Emerging stocks sink to new three-year low\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Romania, Ukraine, Indonesia suspend markets\par \par \uc2 * No international trade in Icelandic crown\par \par \uc2 * Romania \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market\par \par \uc2 * Emerging sovereign debt spreads widest since 2003\par \par \uc2 By Peter Apps\par \par \uc2 LONDON, Oct 10 (Reuters) - Emerging stock markets continued their downward spiral on Friday to a new three-year low having lost over half their value since May, as mounting global market turmoil raised fears of a worldwide recession.\par \par \uc2 Russia, Romania, Ukraine and Indonesia suspended their markets in an attempt to stem the flow, but other markets fell across the board as panicked investors dumped anything seen as risky.\par \par \uc2 Policymakers across emerging markets tried to reassure with limited success. Romania's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to "verify the functioning of the market in the current context of volatility and uncertainty". [nLA291956]\par \par \uc2 The cost of insuring the sovereign debt of Ukraine, Kazakhstan and other Eastern European countries soared, pricing in a mounting risk of default, while there was no international trade of the Icelandic crown <EURISK=D3> after its banking sector, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and economy crashed.\par \par \uc2 "It's a pretty simple story, really," said John Lomax, head of emerging markets equity strategy at \uc2 HSBC\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "This is a combination of risk aversion and immense concern about global growth. It has all gone beyond what seemed predictable. It's very hard to know what to think."\par \par \uc2 Investors are hoping finance chiefs from the Group of Seven industrialised countries meeting in Washington will find a way to stem the crisis, but so far measures from the United States, Britain and other countries have failed to calm credit and money markets or restore confidence.\par \par \uc2 Benchmark emerging equities <.MSCIEF> lost 4.0 percent to a three-year low, now down 52 percent on the year, having been briefly in positive territory as recently as May.\par \par \uc2 Emerging sovereign debt spreads <11EMJ> widened 46 basis points to 592 bps over U.S. Treasuries, their widest levels since May 2003.Spreads were only at 290 basis points over U.S. Treasuries in early August, before war between Russia and Georgia destroyed risk appetite.\par \par \uc2 Most exposed to the credit crunch, Iceland has seen its highly leveraged banks pushed to destruction, leading to nationalisation and a growing row with Britain over the return of deposits in its banks from British savers, including a string of local government bodies.\par \par \uc2 DIPLOMATIC ROW\par \par \uc2 Iceland says it has approached Russia for a loan to cover its banking liabilities, with analysts also speculating over a possible bailout from the International Monetary Fund.\par \par \uc2 Investors are increasingly looking to which country might be next, nervous over other highly indebted banking sectors or countries with wide current account deficits.\par \par \uc2 Prices for five-year debt insurance for Ukrainian debt in the credit default swaps market are pricing roughly an 80 percent risk of default over the next five years, as the country suffers political instability with a looming snap election, rocky relations with Russia and growing macroeconomic problems [nLA77425].\par \par \uc2 CDS prices for Kazakhstan, Latvia, Lithuania, Bulgaria and Romania also widened sharply.\par \par \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Friday it will make forceful efforts to boost domestic demand, saying the country's financial system was safe and stable [ID:nBJC000211]. Analysts fear exports to the west will be hit hard.\par \par \uc2 Russia said it would begin using its reserves to support its stock market from next week, while in a sign of more worries over the banking sector, ratings agency \uc2 Standard & Poor's\uc2  cut the outlook for 13 Russian financial institutions. [nLA278797]\par \par \uc2 India's Finance Minister told television channels there was no need to worry about Indian bank deposits and investors should not panic, saying liquidity in the banking sector would improve once Parliament gave the nod to providing more. [nDEL002022].\par \par \uc2 Polish deputy finance minister Katarzyna Zajdel-Kurowska said the fundamentals of Poland's economy were strong, blaming the overnight decline of the Polish zloty on a slump in Hungary caused by worries over that country's financial system. [nWAR007429].\par \par \uc2 The Hungarian forint <EURHUF=> hit a two-year low, while the zloty <EURPLN=> hit an eight-month low.The rand was at its lowest against the dollar <ZAR=> since late 2002.\par \par \uc2 Central European stock markets were also savaged, with Hungarian equities <.BUX> losing 11 percent and stocks in the Czech Republic <.PX> fell more than 14 percent. (Additional reporting by Carolyn Cohn)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-EMERGING (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|C|D|E|M|O|U|MTL|GRO|SOF|OIL|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020081013e4aa000xa\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
