\par\par \b \uc2 WRAPUP 4-Russia boosts markets support, shares up in London\b0\par\par\uc2 By Olga Popova and Gleb Bryanski   \par \uc2 894 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 September 2008\par 11:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Recasts with Kudrin on share buybacks)\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Sept 18 (Reuters) - Russia said on Thursday it could spend $20 billion on equity purchases as part of an emergency state support totalling $130 billion to stem the worst stock market losses in a decade and ease liquidity worries.\par \par \uc2 The new package of measures, which included a surprise $5.5 billion cut in duties for the oil sector, pushed Russian shares on the London Stock Exchange up 7 percent, with Russia's two main stock exchanges shut for a second day.\par \par \uc2 "The amounts the government talks (about) are indeed dramatic and able to move the market," Raiffeisen Bank said in a note.\par \par \uc2 Money market rates also fell sharply but liquidity concerns remained and yields on government bonds rose to their highest levels in 3-1/2 years as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  again spent billions of dollars to support the rouble.\par \par \uc2 Analysts estimated investors have taken about $36 billion out of Russia since early August, when a brief war with Georgia, combined with a fall in oil prices and global financial turmoil, turned Russian shares from must-have assets into toxic paper.\par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Alexei Kudrin said the state could initiate equity purchases if markets do not stabilise and companies remain undervalued for a long time.\par \par \uc2 "The government has an opportunity ... to start purchases of shares in firms with state participation as well as shares in large reliable companies if stakes are available on the open market," RIA new agency quoted Kudrin as saying.\par \par \uc2 Kudrin, who until the markets crisis had led cabinet opposition to new tax cuts, also said the oil industry would see a cut in export duties to cope with a sharp fall in oil prices.\par \par \uc2 He said the industry, the backbone of the Russian economy, would soon have a bigger tax relief but a decision on a cut in value added tax was put off until 2009.\par \par \uc2 WINFALL REVENUES\par \par \uc2 Ratings agency Standard & Poors has criticised Kudrin for plans to use windfall oil revenues to support the market amid inflation of 15 percent.\par \par \uc2 New measures bring the total amount of promised state support to financial markets to over $130 billion, including 1.5 trillion roubles of budget funds going to banking deposits, 1 trillion available via repo \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  and some 300 billion that banks freed up after a cut in reserve requirements.\par \par \uc2 "For the first time I'm applauding what they (government) did," said Denis Sarantsev, managing director of brokerage UnicreditAton. "It was wise not to reopen the market today ... What we need now is stability"\par \par \uc2 Kudrin said trading on Russian bourses will resume on Friday and top banks would lend $2.4 billion to market players.\par \par \uc2 Russian stocks rose in London with energy firms such as Rosneft closing 22 percent up.\par \par \uc2 The fall in Russia's stock markets since May has been steeper than in many other emerging markets, with many in the market attributing this in part to the increased political risk from \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's military \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Georgia.\par \par \uc2 The domestic political impact has so far been limited because private share ownership in Russia is small, but some analysts say the pressure for greater state \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the markets could derail Medvedev's agenda of liberal reforms.\par \par \uc2 RESCUE MOVE\par \par \uc2 Russia's benchmark RTS is now down around 60 percent from its peak levels in May. Lending between banks nearly dried up this week after problems at medium-sized brokerage Kit Finance sparked speculation there could be bigger victims.\par \par \uc2 The state helped rescue Kit on Wednesday when management firm Leader, part of the business empire of Russian state gas group \uc2 Gazprom\uc2 , said it would buy the brokerage.\par \par \uc2 "(The deal is) very reminiscent of the \uc2 Bear Stearns\uc2  bailout and that too left investors wondering if Russia will have a Lehman-style follow on," said Chris Weafer, chief strategist at brokerage Uralsib.\par \par \uc2 Liquidity injections and a cut in banks' reserve requirement led on Thursday to a decline in money market rates to 8.0 to 8.5 percent from 10.0 to 10.5 percent. Demand at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's repo auctions was below peak levels.\par \par \uc2 But the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market remained tight as dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold yet another $5 billion to keep the rouble steady versus the dollar/euro basket at 30.37.\par \par \uc2 Russian officials say the country's decade-long economic boom and its \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, the world's third largest, insulate it well from the global storm.\par \par \uc2 But reserves have been shrinking fast in the past weeks as the government moved to protect the rouble from capital flight. They fell by a further $13 billion to $560 billion as of Sept. 12, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Rising sovereign risks depressed prices on Russia's benchmark 2030 Eurobond with yields rising to their highest level in 3-1/2 years.\par \par \uc2 When trading in stocks resumes some \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  will still remain suspended, including margin trading, where investors borrow money from the broker, and short selling, or bets on a fall in a stock price, as officials blame such tactics for the market slump. (Additional reporting by Toni Vorobyova; Writing Dmitry Zhdannikov; Editing by David Holmes)\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA-MARKETS/ (WRAPUP 4)|LANGEN|ABX|BNX|FUN|AFA|CSA|LBY|RWSA|RWS|REULB|GNS   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080918e49i000pe\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
