\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Russia c.bank adds words to action, rouble recovers\b0\par\par\uc2 By Dmitry Sergeyev and Andrey Ostroukh   \par \uc2 677 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 September 2008\par 10:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Recasts with rouble reaction, adds details, background, quotes)\par \par \uc2 SOCHI/MOSCOW, Sept 5 (Reuters) - The Russian rouble recovered on Friday from a historic trough after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would not allow the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's trading band to widen, adding further weight to its market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Over the past month investors have fled \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , spooked by disputes over BP's Russian venture \uc2 TNK-BP\uc2  and a government attack on coal miner Mechel as well as the military conflict with Georgia and the subsequent souring of relations with the West.\par \par \uc2 Dealers estimate the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold around $5 billion in the past two day to prop up the rouble, and authorities hammered the message home verbally on Friday.\par \par \uc2 "We are not planning to further widen the boundaries of the corridor in the next few months. For now it suits us," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's first deputy chairman Alexei Ulyukayev told journalists at a banking conference in Sochi, adding that the rouble's recent sell-off was "not critical".\par \par \uc2 The comments sent the rouble to 30.32 against its basket of 0.45 euros and 0.55 dollars, off Thursday's historic low of 30.41. That was the weakest level since the basket's current composition was set 1-1/2 years ago, and also the boundary at which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The (Ulyukayev) statement together with actual \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  suggest that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is drawing a line ... and this may provide support for the basket in the near-term," \uc2 UniCredit\uc2  Aton analysts said in a research note.\par \par \uc2 The rouble's recovery was all the more convincing as Russian stocks continued to sell off, with the benchmark RTS index <.IRTS> breaking through the psychological 1,500 points to hit levels not seen since June 2006.\par \par \uc2 "Money is leaving the equity market, going into dollars. Stabilisation (in the rouble) came after Ulyukayev appeared and explained everything," said Victor Anasimov, dealer at Aljba-Alliance.\par \par \uc2 DRAWING A LINE\par \par \uc2 Ulyukayev estimated Russia had net capital outflows of around $4.6 billion in August and will see zero inflows this month [ID:nL5595478]. Analysts' outflows forecasts are higher.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has so far not allowed the rouble to strengthen beyond 29.26 to the basket, or to weaken beyond 30.41, although it does not disclose its focus corridor.\par \par \uc2 With $582.5 billion of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  and gold reserves as of Monday, it has ample ammunition to support the rouble.\par \par \uc2 The big reserves mean "there is no risk of any \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis in Russia, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will do everything to preserve stability," Kremlin economic aide Arkady Dvorkovich said on Friday at an economics conference in Cernobbio in Italy.\par \par \uc2 "We do not expect any difficulties, even with the substantial capital outflow we've had over the last few weeks."\par \par \uc2 But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also faces a dilemma.\par \par \uc2 On the one hand, allowing greater rouble volatility and showing to investors that it is not a one way appreciation bet is a key step towards its long-term goal of moving to an inflation-targeting regime from one focused on exchange rates.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, a weaker rouble is adding to Russia's inflation headache -- analysts said its depreciation was a key culprit behind a rise in August's inflation that was twice as big as forecast [ID:nL5714172].\par \par \uc2 Any dramatic drop in the rouble's value will also be unpopular. Russians have only recently stopped keeping their savings in dollars and memories of the 1998 finance crisis and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  collapse are still fresh.\par \par \uc2 After the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not step into the market to help the rouble on Wednesday, Russia's business daily Vedomosti headlined its report: "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sacrificed the rouble".\par \par \uc2 -- For a FACTBOX on the rouble's moves see [ID:nL4373729] (Additional reporting by Ian Simpson in Cernobbio, writing by Toni Vorobyova; Editing by Ruth Pitchford)\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA-CBANK/ROUBLE (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080905e495000qc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
