\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Markets-Stocks fall to one-yr low, Ukraine risk up\b0\par\par\uc2 531 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 August 2008\par 12:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Emerging stocks at 12-month low on renewed credit fears\par \par \uc2 * Ukrainian risk premiums rise further on Russia tensions\par \par \uc2 * Commodities retreat pressures Russia, South African stocks * Emerging \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  mostly weaker, Czech crown retreats\par \par \uc2 By Sebastian Tong\par \par \uc2 LONDON, Aug 19 (Reuters) - Emerging shares tumbled to a 12-month low on renewed fears over the health of the global financial system while Ukrainian risk premiums rose further amid persistent geopolitical concerns following Russia's military incursion into Georgia. Global stocks were rattled after a newspaper report said U.S. mortgage giants Fannie Mae and Freddie Mac may be nationalised [ID:nN18494933].\par \par \uc2 Asian stocks fell to a two-year low in the overnight session, little moved by a JPMorgan Chase client note that the Chinese government was considering a $29-58 billion economic stimulus package for Asia's fastest growing economy. [ID:nPEK184422]\par \par \uc2 Resource exporter Russia <.IRTS> suffered the largest equity losses, with its key index falling nearly 4 percent.\par \par \uc2 Retreating commodity prices, which saw oil slip below $112 a barrel, also pressured South Africa stocks <.JTOPI>, which slid 1.65 percent and sent the country's rand \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <ZAR=> down 0.53 percent against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 "You can call it risk aversion, you can call it the global growth story -- it's a combination of small things. Brazil and Russia were big commodity plays and now prices are turning round. Why else should you invest in emerging markets? The justifications are getting thinner and thinner," said Zsolt Papp, chief economist, central and eastern Europe at KBC.\par \par \uc2 By 1050 GMT, the key emerging stock index <.MSCIEF> fell 1.48 percent to 945.83, its lowest level since Aug. 17 2007, while sovereign debt spreads <11EMJ> widened 2 basis points to a month high of 305 bps over U.S. Treasuries.\par \par \uc2 RUSSIAN RISKS\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian sovereign debt spreads were 32 bps wider as investors continued to fret that \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's military \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  into the Georgian breakaway region of South Ossetia signalled a harsher Russian stance against former Soviet countries aspiring to NATO membership.\par \par \uc2 The cost of insuring Ukrainian debt against restructuring or default rose to its highest level since Ukraine's "Orange Revolution" of 2004 with five-year credit default swaps for the country rising 6 bps to close to 467 bps. [ID:nLJ378744] Despite its announcement a withdrawal from Georgia was underway, Russia has yet to pull any of its troops and tanks from its smaller neighbour.\par \par \uc2 A Russian claim that U.S., Polish and Canadian warships were planning to enter the Black Sea is also expected to keep tension high. [ID:nLJ427613]\par \par \uc2 Emerging \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were mostly weaker with the Czech crown <EURCZK=> and the Hungarian forint <EURHUF> both in retreat after both strengthening more than 1 percent on Monday.\par \par \uc2 "Czech central bankers continue to be particularly dovish with a CNB official saying yesterday that another rate cut would be discussed at the coming August meeting...We remain rather negative on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  given the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rhetoric," said BNP Paribas in a research note. (Additional reporting by Carolyn Cohn; )\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-EMERGING|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080822e48j001gc\par }