\par\par \b \uc2 INSTANT VIEW 1-Russia c.bank says to be more active on  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 463 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Mai 2008\par 16:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, May 14 (Reuters) - Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Wednesday it would begin regular \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market as part of transition to an inflation targeting regime.\par \par \uc2 To read the main story click on [ID:nL14841077]\par \par \uc2 SHAHIN VALLEE, EMERGING MARKETS STRATEGIST BNP PARIBAS\par \par \uc2 "There is no corridor at present, there is a spot reference level that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is defending. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  allows the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to move a bit against the spot reference level when it wants to create volatility."\par \par \uc2 "This announcement is quite a big deal, because there have been a lot of rumours about the rouble revaluation.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is creating some uncertainty, it could increase weakness in the short term and shake out positioning, then the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could potentially revalue later. I do not think the fundamentals have changed about the sources of appreciation in the rouble."\par \par \uc2 SERGEI ROMANCHUK, DEALER METALLINVESTBANK\par \par \uc2 "It means the bank will change more often its bid parameters to the basket, but to me it does not mean it is dropping the basket. Today and yesterday we saw some big volatility, which was difficult to explain, and now we can say that was the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  which was buying (dollars). Now there will be days when it will lift the (rouble) to basket and days when it will drop it.\par \par \uc2 NIKOLAI PODGUZOV, ANALYST, RENAISSANCE CAPITAL\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's statement most likely means it wants to increase the rouble volatility to the basket.\par \par \uc2 It will not only bid at the corridor lower level of 29.6 but at higher levels as well to increase the rouble volatility, reduce predictability and reduce speculative mood on the market as far as the rouble level to the basket is concerned.\par \par \uc2 But it does not mean that it will not take a decision to let the rouble appreciate.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is currently trying to switch to interest rates from \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies as a tool to control inflation. It may result in lower speculative capital inflows."\par \par \uc2 DEALER AT A MAJOR FOREIGN BANK\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wants to increase the rouble/basket volatility to reduce speculative pressure it is currently facing, when market players sell the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and go long on the rouble against the basket on rouble appreciation expectations.\par \par \uc2 Should volatility increase, it will force investors to reduce their long positions. Dollar sales to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will fall, it will have to print fewer roubles, which will in turn cut the rouble liquidity and inflation." (Reporting by Carolyn Cohn in London and Andrei Ostroukh in Moscow, Compiled by Dmitry Zhdannikov)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 RUSSIA\b0 \highlight\uc2 -CBANK/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTIONS\b0 \highlight\uc2  (INSTANT VIEW)|LANGEN|C|D|E|M|O|U|MTL|GRO|SOF|OIL   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080517e45e000c0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
