\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Russian gold/ \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  reserves pass $0.5 trln threshold   \b0\par\par\uc2 301 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2008\par 08:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates with analyst quotes, details)   \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, March 20 (Reuters) - Russia's gold and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves have passed the $0.5 trillion threshold, rising to $502.1 billion on March 14 from $494.5 billion on March 7, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showed on Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 The figure suggested the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has resumed its purchases of petrodollars in the market in March as prices for oil, Russia's main export commodity, hit record highs on speculative demand and supply uncertainty.   \par \par \uc2 Analysts estimated the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has already bought about $10 billion in March after it only \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  three or four times in January-February, buying about $2 billion in these two months amid net capital outflows.   \par \par \uc2 The inflow of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from energy exports in March has neutralised capital outflows, expected to net at about $9 billion, forcing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to resume its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's reserves are the world's third largest.   \par \par \uc2 "The inflow of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is so big, the price for oil is so high, that it beats everything," said Yevgeny Nadorshin, analyst at Trust Bank, suggesting Russia has returned to its 'natural' state of reserve growth of the past few years.   \par \par \uc2 "It is positive for liquidity. It is positive for interest rates," Nadorshin said, adding renewed \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  inflows would flood the money market with liquidity, badly needed by banks and corporations that have foreign debt.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  expects a liquidity shortage in the next few weeks, with the daily refinancing demand from banks hitting 400 billion roubles in April. Currently, money market rates <RUBOND=> are around 3.25-4.20 percent. (Reporting by Gleb Bryanski; Editing by Ruth Pitchford)   \par \par \uc2 RUSSIA-CBANK/RESERVES (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080320e43k000e2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
