\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3-Russia's RTS index down, rouble weakens   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Gleb Bryanski and Olga Popova   \par \uc2 701 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Januar 2008\par 09:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Releads, updates market data after close)   \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Jan 22 (Reuters) - Russian stocks and the rouble pared heavy intraday losses on Tuesday as blue chips outperformed other emerging markets, but traders said a sharp cut in U.S. interest rates did little to change a gloomy outlook.   \par \par \uc2 Analysts said they believe Russia is better positioned to weather the global storm than other emerging markets. The rouble also recovered in late trading in Moscow after dipping close to a level below which \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be expected.   \par \par \uc2 "Do not panic, \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  is no Turkey. The rouble still makes Russia a relative safe haven," analysts at Troika Dialog brokerage wrote in a research note.   \par \par \uc2 "The key markets at risk from the current bout of panic over the U.S. growth are those with expensive \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  funded by foreign capital. With its strong macro backdrop, Russia is not subject to this risk," Troika analysts said.   \par \par \uc2 The RTS stock index <.IRTS> ended down 1.61 percent at 1967.7 points. It had earlier fallen briefly below 1,900 points for the first time since September 2007, before rebounding into positive territory above 2,000 points.   \par \par \uc2 The turnover on Russia's biggest bourse, MICEX's equity section, was a healthy 131.7 billion roubles ($5.29 billion).   \par \par \uc2 The U.S. Federal Reserve cut its interest rates by a dramatic 75 basis points, in a move usually reducing the flight to safer assets, such as government bonds in rich economies.   \par \par \uc2 "First there was euphoria (after the Fed decision). The market spiked up, but then started sliding again," said Pavel Vashchenko from trading company IK Region.   \par \par \uc2 "We see it could not impress the market, which will continue to be driven by the same negative factors," he said.   \par \par \uc2 Russian stocks outperformed other emerging markets for most of the day, but by 1608 GMT were marginally worse. The MSCI Russia index <.MIRU00000PUS> fell 2.9 percent versus a 2.5 percent slide in the MSCI Emerging Markets index <.MSCIEF>.   \par \par \uc2 Former electricity monopoly Unified Energy System led the fall with a 4.0 percent decline, while state oil major Rosneft fell by 3.4 percent.   \par \par \uc2 But not all stocks ended down. Gazprom , the world's largest gas producer and one of the world's 10 largest stocks, climbed 1.1 percent, and mining giant Norilsk Nickel was up 1.9 percent.   \par \par \uc2 Russia's 2008 budget is balanced at an average oil price of $53 per barrel, and analysts see no major external threats to macroeconomic stability if the oil price stays above this level. U.S. crude <CLc1> was trading at $88.19 a barrel by 1510 GMT.   \par \par \uc2 ROUBLE CLOSE TO MINIMUM LEVEL   \par \par \uc2 The rouble weakened about 0.4 percent to 29.82 against the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar/euro \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket made of 0.55 dollars and 0.45 euros as of 0800 GMT and dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not seen on the market.   \par \par \uc2 The rouble <RUBUTSTN=MCX> weakened to 24.92 to the dollar, which accounts for the lion's share of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trade on the Russian market, but then climbed back to 24.75.   \par \par \uc2 "We believe that the rouble is close to its minimum level and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unlikely to allow it to weaken further," said Stanislav Ponomarenko, head of research at ING in Moscow.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which runs the world's third-largest gold and \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, does not comment on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves.   \par \par \uc2 OFFERINGS POSTPONED   \par \par \uc2 Analysts said the market turbulence would affect Russian companies' plans to float stocks and raise debt.   \par \par \uc2 "It is clear that all offerings scheduled for the next month will be postponed. The first quarter outlook is more blurred. A lot will depend on the situation in the United States," said Oleg Lukhton, head of investment banking at Uralsib.   \par \par \uc2 Russian Eurobonds remained stable with the 2030 bond <0#RU011428878=> trading with a spread of 184 basis points against the U.S. treasuries. (Reporting by Gleb Bryanski and Olga Popova; Editing by Jason Neely; Editing by Paul Bolding)   \par \par \uc2 RUSSIA-RTS/ (UPDATE 3)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|D|M|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080122e41m000kf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
