\par\par \b \uc2 Russian markets -- Factors to Watch on Dec 6   \b0\par\par\uc2 698 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Dezember 2007\par 08:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Dec 6 (Reuters) - Here are events and news stories that could move Russian markets today.   \par \par \uc2 You can reach us on: +7 495 775 1242   \par \par \uc2 STOCKS CALL (Contributions to moscow.newsroom@reuters.com):   \par \par \uc2 Troika Dialog: Opens prices up 0.5 percent as markets in Asia, except China, trade higher and after U.S. stocks surged on increased productivity and an employment report that suggested the economy might avoid a recession. Aton: Expects markets to open up 0.5 percent, although oil stocks might not fare as well as yesterday.   \par \par \uc2 EVENTS [RU-DIA] (All times GMT):   \par \par \uc2 * MOSCOW - Cabinet Meeting. Russian Finance Minister Alexei Kudrin and Economy Minister Elvira Nabiullina to speak   \par \par \uc2 * BRUSSELS - Polish Foreign Minister Radoslaw Sikorski expected to meet Russian counterpart Sergei Lavrov   \par \par \uc2 * MOSCOW - Dresdner Kleinwort Bank holds press conference   \par \par \uc2 * MOSCOW - The 4th Annual Forum entitled "Mergers and Acquisitions in Russia"   \par \par \uc2 * LONDON - Training Course "Managing Risks in Banks" as part of the Russian Banking Forum   \par \par \uc2 * ST PETERSBURG - Russian Bond Congress 2007 (to Dec 7).   {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.cbonds.info/eng/bondcongress/spb2007/agenda.phtml"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.cbonds.info/eng/bondcongress/spb2007/agenda.phtml  }}}\par \par \uc2 * AMSTERDAM - Conference entitled "Asset Management in Russia and CIS" (to Dec 7).   \par \par \uc2 * MOSCOW - International Conference entitled "Russian Petroleum Product Market: Exports and Domestic Sales" (to Dec 7).   {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://products.oil-tr.ru/Default.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://products.oil-tr.ru/Default.aspx  }}}\par \par \uc2 * MOSCOW - Sitronics Q3 results and conference call (1330)   \par \par \uc2 * MOSCOW - \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to auction 5 billion roubles of Series 3 OBR bills <RU0A0JPDX9=MM>   \par \par \uc2 IN THE PAPERS [PRESS/RU]:   \par \par \uc2 Vedomosti business daily reports a strong day for Russian stock markets on its front page. The RTS index climbed 2.6 percent on good news from  \uc2 Gazprom\uc2  and rumours the country's sovereign rating could soon be raised.   \par \par \uc2 RBC Daily carries an interview with  \uc2 E.ON\uc2  Chief Executive Wulf Bernotat, who says electricity will not become any cheaper.   \par \par \uc2 TOP STORIES IN RUSSIA AND THE CIS [RU-NEWS]:   \par \par \uc2 TOP NEWS:    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Prosecutors turn up heat on Russia's Storchak    [ID:nL05309149]\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 Gazprom\f28 \uc2 \f2  Q2 net profit falls, misses forecast      [ID:nL0521059]\par Third term for Putin would not faze most Russians[ID:nL05296641]\par  \par  COMPANIES/MARKETS:\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 Russian Copper Co\f28 \uc2 \f2  plans IPO by 2010 - source     [ID:nL06620539]\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Russia Mercury acquires control of retailer Dixy [ID:nL06722209] Russia UES delays TGK-4 SALE AT bidders' request [ID:nL05711166] Russia's Atomenergomash to invest $1 bln in 2 yrs [ID:nL0526158] Russia Onexim prefers Norilsk stake sale to RUSAL[ID:nL05443749] Kazakh ENRC IPO oversubscribed at top end-source [ID:nL05633264] Gazprombank opens credit line for Power Machines [ID:nL05519207]   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ECONOMY/POLITICS: Russian gold/\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves rise to $463.5 bln [ID:nMSK000218] Russia to issue 1.7 trln rbls in bonds in 2008-10[ID:nL05154341]    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Russia Nov CPI up 1.2 pct m/m, above forecasts    [ID:nL0579829]\par Russia Nov GDP growth +6.3 pct y/y-survey         [ID:nL0569520]\par Russia c.bank injects