\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Russian c.bank seen buying dollars after CPI data   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Gleb Bryanski and Yelena Fabrichnaya   \par \uc2 629 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Oktober 2007\par 15:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Releads on c.bank \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 )   \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Oct 5 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen actively buying dollars on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Friday after the release of higher-than-expected inflation data, traders told Reuters.   \par \par \uc2 Russia's consumer price index (CPI) rose by 0.8 percent month-on-month in September, the Federal Statistics Service (FSS) said, significantly exceeding analysts' expectations.   \par \par \uc2 "Market players expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to appreciate the rouble against the dual \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket in order to lower inflationary pressure. They have opened long positions in the rouble," a Moscow bank dealer told Reuters.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  controls inflation through the rouble exchange rate and uses a dual \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket, made up of 0.55 dollars and 0.45 euros, to guide its \b \highlight22\uc2 forex interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 A stronger rouble makes imported goods cheaper but impacts the inflation rate only with a time lag of several months. Analysts have said any exchange rate move by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  now is unlikely to influence the full-year inflation rate.   \par \par \uc2 Traders said they believed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had bought between $2.5 and $3.0 billion by 1250 GMT. The rouble remained stable against the dollar/euro \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket.   \par \par \uc2 HORRIBLE FIGURE   \par \par \uc2 The CPI rise follows massive liquidity injections into the banking sector by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and suggests Russia may significantly overshoot its annual inflation target of 8.0 percent.   \par \par \uc2 "This is a horrible figure. I do not remember a time when expectations and reality were so different. It means it will even be difficult to have the same inflation as last year's 9 percent," said Natalya Orlova, economist at  \uc2 Alfa Bank.\par \par \uc2 Some analysts said the current liquidity squeeze gives the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  more leverage over inflation through its interest rates policy -- a major shift in Russia's monetary policy, which was aimed at tackling excess liquidity in recent years. "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  now has considerably greater latitude to use interest rate policy to address inflation, since it is supplying liquidity to the banking system," said Rory MacFarquhar, senior economist at  \uc2 Goldman Sachs.\par \par \uc2 POLICY FAILURE   \par \par \uc2 The September rise brings price growth in the first nine months of the year to 7.5 percent, for the first time in 2007 exceeding last year's corresponding figure. The CPI grew by 7.2 percent in the same period of 2006.   \par \par \uc2 Officials as well as analysts polled by Reuters had expected the CPI index to rise 0.4 percent.   \par \par \uc2 "This is a very unpleasant surprise for the government. It puts it in a situation when measures aimed to support liquidity levels in the banking system contradict anti-inflation measures," said Yulia Tsepliaeva from  \uc2 Merrill Lynch.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  provided banks with billions of roubles of liquidity in August and September after a global credit crunch shut sources of cheap financing abroad.   \par \par \uc2 Russia had 9 percent inflation in 2006, after raising the annual target and introducing tough anti-inflation measures, including the rouble appreciation.   \par \par \uc2 Kremlin economic aide Arkady Dvorkovich told Reuters last month that an overshoot above last year's figure would represent policy failure.   \par \par \uc2 The FSS said core inflation, an indicator cleared of seasonal and volatile factors, rose 1.6 percent in September. The spike in core inflation suggests monetary factors were the main culprit behind the surprisingly high figure.   \par \par \uc2 Food prices jumped 1.0 percent due to increases in prices for milk, dairy products and sunoil. Russian dairy producers said last month prices for milk powder and raw milk spiked in Russia due to a soaring global demand for milk products. (Additional reporting by Yelena Fabrichnaya and Maria Kiselyova)   \par \par \uc2 RUSSIA-CPI (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020071005e3a5001c4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
