\par\par \b \uc2 INSTANT VIEW 5-Putin dismisses Russia PM ahead of elections   \b0\par\par\uc2 619 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 September 2007\par 14:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Sept 12 (Reuters) - Russian President Vladimir Putin dismissed his prime minister on Wednesday, clearing the way for him to appoint a new premier who is likely to become the leading candidate in presidential elections next March.   \par \par \uc2 COMMENTARY:   \par \par \uc2 ROLAND NASH, HEAD OF RESEARCH, RENAISSANCE CAPITAL:   \par \par \uc2 "The speculation is that (First Deputy Prime Minister Sergei) Ivanov will be appointed prime minister and the next prime minister will be the next president of Russia between 2008 and 2012. That's the consensus and we agree with the consensus.   \par \par \uc2 "The market consensus is: Ivanov bad, (First Deputy Prime Minister Dmitry) Medvedev good, so the markets might take an Ivanov appointment badly.   \par \par \uc2 "But in my view Ivanov represents the clearest continuity to Putin, during whose tenure Russian stocks gained $1 trillion in value. Putin has been obsessed with an orderly transition, and the precedent was set with his own appointment as prime minister (in 1999)."   \par \par \uc2 SERGEI MARKOV, HEAD OF INSTITUTE FOR POLITICAL STUDIES:   \par \par \uc2 "I think the candidacy of the prime minister will be a political appointment," Markov told the Vesti-24 TV news channel.   \par \par \uc2 "Sergei Ivanov is candidate No.1 and Dmitry Medevedev is candidate No.2. But there is always the possibility for something unexpected as Putin has shown before that he can surprise people.   \par \par \uc2 "Probably the (next prime minister) will become the (Kremlin's) candidate for the presidency but it could equally be that this person will work as the partner of the next president and will remain as prime minister under the new president in order to ensure continuity for Putin's policies."   \par \par \uc2 CHRIS WEAFER, STRATEGIST, URALSIB:   \par \par \uc2 "Share prices weakened a bit, because markets hate uncertainty.   \par \par \uc2 "The choice (of prime minister) is pretty much between (First Deputy Prime Minister Sergei) Ivanov and (Deputy Prime Minister Sergei) Naryshkin. Whichever one is named as prime minister will be in the prime slot to become the next president.   \par \par \uc2 "We see the next presidency as an interruption, rather than a new direction. (President Vladimir) Putin is looking to carve out a role where he remains very much involved in the process, giving the option to come back later.   \par \par \uc2 "There will be a seamless transition. The course for 2008 and 2009 is in place and frankly it doesn't matter for that period who the president is. What will matter is where Putin is positioned when the more difficult issues have to be addressed at mid-term."   \par \par \uc2 ALEXANDER KARPOV, \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2  DEALER, ZENIT BANK:   \par \par \uc2 "There was some short-term impact of this news on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. Someone tried to buy dollars, weakening the rouble slightly. Everyone understands that there is no crisis in the economy and this news is not related to the economic situation."   \par \par \uc2 OLEG VYUGIN, MDM BANK CHAIRMAN, FORMER HEAD OF FINANCIAL MARKETS WATCHDOG:   \par \par \uc2 "I do not think this will have a big impact on the markets. Such a scenario has been discussed. It was not clear when it will happen. Obviously it is the preparation for the election. What is interesting is who will head the new government. That is what the markets will be waiting for."   \par \par \uc2 STANISLAV PONOMARENKO, ANALYST AT ING BANK, MOSCOW:   \par \par \uc2 "If everything with the new appointments resolves itself quickly, we do not expect it to have a major impact on the economy."   \par \par \uc2 MARKET REACTION:   \par \par \uc2 Russia's benchmark RTS index <.IRTS> is down 0.41 percent on the day. The rouble <RUB=> is flat against the dual \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket, used by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to guide \b \highlight22\uc2 forex interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 LINKS:   \par \par \uc2 - For all \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  news and data, 3000 Xtra users can click on: <RUSSIA>   \par \par \uc2 RUSSIA-FRADKOV/INSTANT (INSTANT VIEW 5)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|G   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070912e39c001cg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
